Anu, son of Yayāti. § 144 (Yayāti): I, 75, 3160, 3162 (did not take upon himself his father's decrepitude), (v. Nahusha).--§ 147 (Devayānī): I, 83, 3433 (son of Śarmishṭhā).--§ 148e: I, 84, Yayāti cursed his older sons; Anu should be overcome by decrepitude and not be able to perform sacrifices before Agni, and his progeny should die as soon as they attained to youth: I, 84, 3488 (3489); his sons were the Mlecchāḥ: I, 85, 3520, 3533.--§ 156 (Pūruv.): I, 95, 3762.

