बाल्हीक
Bālhī¤ka^3 ([great-]grandson of the elder Dhṛtarāshṭra and son of Pratīpa, and brother of Devāpi and Śāntanu). § 155 (Pūruv.): I, 94, 3750, 3751 (is made king together with Śāntanu).--§ 156 (do.): I, 95, 3797 (son of Pratīpa and Śaibyā Sunandā).--§ 194 (Pāṇḍu): I, 126, 4911 (Somadatto 'tha Bºḥ).--§ 208 (Astradarśana): I, 134, 5313 (Kṛpasya, Somadattasya, Bāhlīkasya ca dhīmataḥ…sānnidhye).-§ 213 (Jatugṛhap.): I, 143, 5707 (Droṇaṃ ca Bālhi¤kañ caiva Somadattañ ca Kauravaṃ).--§ 287 (Rājasūyikap.): II, 34, 1266 (tathā Śalyaś ca bhagavān Bāhlikaś ca mahābalaḥ | Somadatto 'tha Kauravyo Bhūrir Bhūriśravāḥ Śalaḥ).-§ 288 (do.): II, 35, 1293 (Bāhliko Dhṛtarāshṭraś ca, Somadatto Jayadrathaḥ | Nakulena samānītāḥ svāmivat tatra remire).-§ 296 (Dyūtap.): II, 53, 1912 (Vāhlīko ratham āhārshīd jāmbūnada-vibhūshitaṃ).--§ 298 (do.): II, 58, 2011 (Bālhīkena rathaṃ yattaṃ [i.e. dattaṃ, cf. 1912]); 63, 2112 (Prātipeyāḥ Śāntanavā Bhīmasenāḥ sa-Vāhlikāḥ | Duryodhanāparā-dhena kṛcchraṃ prāpsyanti sarvaśaḥ).--§ 302 (Anudyūtap.): II, 74, 2477 (tato Droṇaḥ, Somadatto, Vāhlīkaś caiva, Gautamaḥ… in vain dissuaded the game).--§ 305 (Anudyūtap.): II, 78, 2560 (Yudhishṭhira said: āmantrayāmi Bharatāṃs tathā vṛddhaṃ pitāmahaṃ | rājānaṃ Somadattañ ca mahārājañ ca Vāhlikaṃ).--§ 307 (do.): II, 81, 2697 (Dhṛtarāshṭra related: prātishṭhata tato Bhīshmo Droṇena saha Sañjaya | Kṛpaś ca Somadattaś ca Vāhlīkaś ca mahā-manāḥ).--§ 318 (Arjunābhigamanap.): III, 13, 599 (among the means of dissuading Dhṛtarāshṭra from permitting the game, Kṛshṇa mentioned Bhīshma-Droṇau samānāyya Kṛpaṃ Vāhlīkam eva ca).--§ 512 (Ghoshayātrāp.): III, 249, 15084 (Duryodhana asked Karṇa: “What will Bhīshma, Droṇa, Kṛpa, Drauṇi, Vidura, Sañjaya, Vāhli¤ka, Saumadatti, etc., say to me when I come to Hāstinapura?”).--§ 514 (Ghoshayātrāp.): III, 252, 15205 (Bhūriśravāḥ, Somadatto, mahārājaś ca Vāhlikaḥ…Kurūdvahāḥ followed Duryodhana; kālenālpena rājendra sva-puraṃ viviśus tadā).--§ 515 (Karṇadigvijaya): III, 254, 15261 (Duryodhana said to Karṇa when the latter had fulfilled his Digvijaya: “What I have not been able to accomplish through Bhīshma, Droṇa, Kṛpa, and Vāhlika, I have obtained through thee”).--§ 552 (Goharaṇap.): IV, 38, 1243 (Uttara said about the Kuru army: yatra Droṇaś ca Bhīshmaś ca Kṛpaḥ Karṇo Viviṃśatiḥ | Aśvatthāmā Vikarṇaś ca Somadattaś ca Vāhlikaḥ, etc.).--§ 556 (Sañjayayānap.): V, 23, †693 (Yudhishṭhira asked Sañjaya about the health of Bhīshma, Dhṛtarāshṭra, mahārājo Vāhlikaḥ Prātipeyaḥ…vidvān, Somadatta, Bhūriśravas, etc.); 30, †885 (Yudhishṭhira asked Sañjaya to salute Droṇa, Aśvatthāman, Kṛpa, etc., sa Vāhlikānām ṛshabho manīshī, who never cherishes any other wish than that there should be peace among the Bharatas, and Somadatta, Saumadatti, etc.).--§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 47, 1796 (Bhīshma, Droṇa, Kṛpa, Śalya, Kṛtavarman, Jayadratha, Aśvatthāman, Vikarṇa, Somadatta, Vāhlika, Vidura, Dhṛtarāshṭra, etc., entered the hall for hearing the message of Sañjaya); 55, 2206 (the chief warriors of the Kurus are Bhīshma, Droṇa, Kṛpa, etc., Drauṇi, Vaikartana Karṇa, Somadatta, Vāhlika, Prāgjyotishādhipaḥ, Śalya, Āvantyo, 'tha Jayadrathaḥ, etc.); 57, 2289 (Sañjaya should inform sa-Vāhlikān Kurūn… Prātipeyān Śaradvataḥ, etc.); 58, 2300 (Dhṛtarāshṭra, Vāhlika, Bhīshma, Droṇa, Aśvatthāman, Sañjaya, Somadatta, Śala, and Kṛpa, etc., do not wish the combat), , 2304 (Duryodhana will challenge the Pāṇḍavas without depending upon Dhṛtarāshṭra, Droṇa, Aśvatthāman, Sañjaya, Bhīshma, Kāmboja, Kṛpa, Vāhlika, etc.); 62, †2426 (Karṇa boasts that he will slay myriads of warriors in the sight of Āvantya-KāliṅgaJayadratheshu…Vāhlike ca); 63, 2432 (Duryodhana says that he is not dependent on Bhīshma, Droṇa, Kṛpa, Vāhlika, etc.); 65, 2493 (Dhṛtarāshṭra exhorts Duryodhana to follow himself, Droṇa, Kṛpa, Vikarṇa, Bhīshma, mahārājañ ca Vāhlikaṃ); 66, 2501 (Arjuna had said that Bhīshma, Dhṛtarāshṭra, Sañjaya, Droṇa, Kṛpa, Karṇa, mahārājañ ca Vāhlikaṃ, etc., were in the greatest danger).--§ 562 (Bhagavadyānap.): V, 80, 2859 (Vidura, Bhīshma, Droṇaś ca saha-Vāhlikaḥ will understand Kṛshṇa); 83, 2966 (Yudhishṭhira tells Kṛshṇa to salute Bhīshma, Droṇa, Kṛpa, mahārājañ ca Vāhlikaṃ, Drauṇi, Somadatta, etc.); 89, 3114 (Kṛpa, Somadatta, mahārājaś ca Vāhlikaḥ rose from their seats and honoured Kṛshṇa), 3117() (Kṛshṇa accosted Droṇaṃ sa-Vāhlīkaṃ sa-putrañ ca, Kṛpa, and Somadatta); 90, 3180 (Dhṛtarāshṭra, mahārājaś ca Vāhli¤kaḥ, Kṛpa, Somadatta, and the Kurus had grieved at the dragging of Kṛshṇā at the game); 91, 3271 (Droṇa, Kṛpa, Bhīshmo, 'tha Vāhlikaḥ, and [the]<BR>Kurus came to Kṛshṇa); 95, 3402 (Duryodhana will be irresistible, when he has Bhīshma, Droṇa, Kṛpa, Karṇa, Viviṃśati, Aśvatthāman, Vikarṇa, Somadatto, 'tha Vāhlikaḥ, etc.).--§ 567 (do.): V, 124, 4138 (Duryodhana does not follow Dhṛtarāshṭra, Bhīshma, Droṇa, Vidura, Kṛpa, Somadattasya, Vāhlīkasya ca dhīmataḥ, etc.); 128, 4284 (Duryodhana disregards Vidura, Dhṛtarāshṭra, mahārājañ ca Vāhlikaṃ, etc.); 129, 4350 (Bhīshma, Dhṛtarāshṭra, and Vāhlika have given their share to the sons of Pāṇḍu from fear of disunion); 131, 4453 (Kṛshṇa addressed Dhṛtarāshṭra, Droṇa, Bhīshma, Vidura, Vāhlika, and Kṛpa), 4457() (Kṛshṇa was followed by Bhīshma, Droṇa, Kṛpa, Vidura, Dhṛtarāshṭra, Vāhlika, etc.).--§ 569 (do.): V, 149, 5055, 5059, 5066, 5067 (V. abandoned his father and brother and obtained the wealthy kingdom of his maternal uncle, permitting Śāntanu to rule the paternal kingdom).--§ 570 (Sainyaniryānap.): V, 155, 5275 (among the eleven men, Kṛpa, Droṇa, etc., under each of whom Duryodhana placed an akshauhiṇī).--§ 572 (Rathātirathas.): V, 167, 5797 (is an atiratha).--§ 576 (Bhagavadgītāp.): VI, 17, 675 (the Kuru army was arrested by Droṇa, Bhīshma, Aśvatthāman, Vāhlīka, and Kṛpa).--§ 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 45^10, 1707 (fights Dhṛshtaketu = Cedirājaḥ, 1709), 1709; 48, 1925^34 (he attacked Śveta with Kṛṭavarman, Kṛpa, Śalya, Jārāsandhi, Vikarṇa, and Viviṃśati in order to protect Bhīshma).--§ 580 (do.): VI, 59, †2643 (at sunset the Kurus sa-Bhīshmāḥ, sa-Droṇa-Duryodhana-Vāhlikāś ca, withdrew their troops), †2648 (Droṇa, Kṛpa, Saindhava-Vāhlikau, Bhūriśravas, Śalya-Śalau, etc., were vanquished by Arjuna). --§ 581 (do.): VI, 60, 2652 (Droṇa, Duryodhana, Vāhlika, etc., accompanied Bhīshma).--§ 583 (do.): VI, 76, 3330 (the Kuru army was protected by Droṇa, Bhīshma, Kṛtavarman, Kṛpa, Duḥśāsana, Jayadratha, etc., Bhagadatta, Vikarṇa, Drauṇi, Saubala, and Vāhlika).--§ 584 (do.): VI, 81, 3533 (Bhīshma said to Duryodhana that he, Droṇa, Śalya, etc., Vāhlikaḥ saha Vāhlikaiḥ, etc., would fight for him).--§ 585 (do.): VI, 92, 4118 (Bhīshma sent Droṇa, Somadatta, Vāhliko, 'tha Jayadrathaḥ, etc., to the rescue of Duryodhana), 4129 (was wounded by Ghaṭotkaca); 96, 4340 (with Kṛtavarman he fought Sātyaki).--§ 586 (do.): VI, 102, 4666 (Aśvatthāman, Śalya, Kāmbojaś ca Sudakshiṇaḥ | Vindānuvindāv Āvantyau, Vāhlikaḥ saha Vāhlikaiḥ, surrounded Arjuna); 104, 4746 (fought Bhīmasena: Bhīmasenas tu rājānaṃ Vāhlikaṃ prapitāmahaṃ | viddhvānadan mahā-nādaṃ…), 4753, 4754 (mounted upon the chariot of Lakshmaṇa).--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakav.): VII, 20, 800 (Bhūriśravas, Śalya, Somadatta, and Vāhlika were in the right wing of Droṇa's Garuḍa-array on the twelfth day of the battle); 25, 1081 (fought Drupada); 32, 1373 (fought Bhīmasena); 39, 1660 (Duryodhana told Karṇa, Vāhlika, etc., to crush Abhimanyu). --§ 596 (Pratijñāp.): VII, 74, 2619 (Jayadratha said that not even Droṇa, Duryodhana, Kṛpa, Karṇa-Madreśa-Vāhlikāḥ, etc., could protect him).--§ 598 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 85, 3043 (Dhṛtarāshṭra said that the Pāṇḍavas would hear Śalya, Somadatta, Bhīshma, Droṇa, Vikarṇa, Vāhlīka, Kṛpa, etc.).--§ 599 (Jayadrathav.): VII, 95, 3527 (Vāhlīka-rājas tejasvī kulaputra mahārathaḥ…Draupadeyān avārayat), 3534 (fought Śikhaṇḍin); 96, 3548, 3549 (fought Śikhaṇḍin), 3553 (Vāhlīka-rājaḥ, fought the Draupadeyas).--§ 600 (Ghaṭotkacavadhap.): VII, 155, 6720 (in the sight of Karṇa, Drauṇi, Duryodhana, Kṛpa, Somadatta, and Vāhlīka, Bhīmasena s