Śālvāyana, adj. (“belonging to the Śālvas”). § 273 (Rājasūyārambhap.): II, 14, 591 (rājānaḥ, fled from fear of Jarāsandha).

शाल्वेय
Śālveya, pl. (ºāḥ), a people. § 522 (Draupadīharaṇap.): III, 264, 15576 (desirous of matrimony, the Sindhu king Jayadratha is going to the Ś.).--§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 54, 2138 (have sided with Yudhishṭhira).--§ 599 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 98, 3662 (ºsenāḥ, attack Droṇa). Cf. Śālva, pl., and the next.

