शिव
Śiva^2, name of a lac-house. § 213 (Jatugṛhap.): I, 146, 5778 (nivedayām āsa gṛhaṃ Śºākhyam aśivaṃ tadā, sc. Purocana).

शिव
Śiva^3, a fire. § 490 (Āṅgirasa): III, 221, 14177, 14178 (v. Aśiva).

शिव
Śiva^4 = Kṛshṇa: VI, 3010; XII, 1863.

शिव
Śiva^5, pl. (ºāḥ). § 317b (Kṛshṇa Vāsudeva); III, 12, 513 (ºānām īśvareśvara, i.e. Kṛshṇa).--§ 565 (Gālavac.): V, 109, 3796 (atra--i.e. in the south--siddhāḥ Śivā nāma brāhmaṇā vedapāragāḥ | adhītya sakalān Vedān lebhire moksham avyayaṃ, so B.; for the reading of C. v. Śivā^3).

शिवा
Śivā^1, wife of the Vasu Anila. § 116 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 66, 2589 (wife of Anila and mother of Manojava and Avijñātagati).

शिवा
Śivā^2, wife of Aṅgiras. § 496 (Skandotpatti): III, 225, 14299 (bharyā tv Aṅgirasaḥ, Svahā assumed her form), 14301 (do.), (14303) (i.e. Svāhā), 14305 (do., cohabited with Agni).

शिवा
Śivā^3, a brāhmaṇī. § 565 (Gālavac.): V, 109, 3796 (C. atra--i.e. in the south--siddhā Śivā nāma brāhmaṇī vedapāragā | adhītya sakalān Vedān lebhe sandeham akshayaṃ; for the reading of B. v. Śiva, pl.).

शिवा
Śivā^4, a river. § 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 332 (in Bhāratavarsha).

शिवकर्णी
Śivakarṇī, a mātṛ. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2647.

शिवपुर
Śivapura (“the city of Śiva”). § 377 (Dhaumyatīrthak.): III, 88, 8334 (having beheld the image of Śūlin--i.e. Śiva-at Payoshṇī, one attains to Ś.).

शिवि
Śivi^1--3, Śiviputra, Śivisūnu, so C. for Śibº, q.v.

शिवोद्भेद
Śivodbheda, name of a place. § 360 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 82, 5053 (there the river Sarasvatī reappears), 5054.

श्मशानभाज्
Śmaśānabhāj = Śiva (1000 names^2).

श्मशानवासिन्
Śmaśānavāsin = Śiva: X, 254; XIII, 1147 (1000 names^2).

शोभन
Śobhana = Śiva (1000 names^2).

शोभना
Śobhanā, a mātṛ. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2624.

शोकनाशन
Śokanāśana = Vishṇu (1000 names).

शोण
Śoṇa, a river. § 268 (Varuṇasabhāv.): II, 9, 373 (among the rivers in Varuṇa's palace).--§ 276 (Jarāsandhavadhap.): II, 20, 796 (crossed by Kṛshṇa, etc., on their way from Indraprastha to Rājagṛha).--§ 370 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 85, 8150 (ºsya Jyotirathyāyāś ca saṅgame), 8151 (ºsya Narmadāyāś ca prabhave (B. prabhede) …Vaṃśagulme).--§ 459 (Mārkaṇḍeyas.): III, 188, 12910 (seen by Mārkaṇḍeya in the stomach of Nārāyaṇa).--§ 494 (Āṅgirasa): III, 222, 14233 (among the rivers who are mothers of fires).--§ 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 337 (enumeration of the rivers of Bhāratavarsha; both C. and B. have Śoṇāṃ).

शोणाश्व
Śoṇāśva, Śoṇāśvavāha, Śoṇahaya = Droṇa, q.v.

शोणितभृत्
Śoṇitabhṛt = Kṛshṇa: XIII, 7367.

शोणितोद
Śoṇitoda, a Yaksha. § 269 (Vaiśravaṇasabhāv.): II, 10, 399 (in the palace of Kubera).

श्रद्धा
Śraddhā^1 (‘Faith’), daughter of Daksha and wife of Dharma. § 115 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 66, 2578.

श्रद्धा
Śraddhā^2 (do.), daughter of Vivasvat. § 680b (TulādhāraJājali-saṃv.): XII, 265, 9449 (Vaivasvatī Sūryasya duhitā Sāvitṝ, cf. the allegoric explanation of Nīl.), 9450.

श्राद्धदेव
Śrāddhadeva^1 = Manu: XII, 4507.

श्राद्धदेव
Śrāddhadeva^2 = Vivasvat: XII, ††13219 (Mārttaṇḍo Vivasvān).

श्राद्धपर्वन्
Śrāddhaparvan (ºva), “the section relating to the Śrāddha,” the 87th of the minor parvans of Mhbhr. § 10 (Parvas.): I, 2, 349.--§ 620: Kṛshṇa censured Gāndhārī, saying that this vast carnage had taken place by her fault, through her son Duryodhana; and told her not to grieve (“the cow brings forth offspring to bear burthens… the Śūdrā woman to increase the number of servitors… a princess, like thee, brings forth sons to be slaughtered”). Gāndhārī remained silent. Requested by Dhṛtarāshṭra, Yudhishṭhira said that one billion 660,020,000 men had fallen; and 24,165 had escaped; the fallen had all attained to regions like those of Indra (specifying those who had attained to G., Gh., Brahmaloka, and Uttarakurus). Yudhishṭhira said that in the forest he had obtained the gift of spiritual vision from D.-ṛ. Lomaśa. Urged by Dhṛtarāshṭra, Yudhishṭhira ordered Sudharman, etc. (), to cause the funeral rites of the slain () to be duly performed; they burned them upon funeral pyres; the Pitṛmedha-rites were performed for some of the illustrious dead; by the noise of sāmans, ṛcs, and lamentations all creatures became stupefied that night. Then Yudhishṭhira and Dhṛtarāshṭra proceeded towards the Gaṅgā (XI, 26). The Kuru ladies, etc., performed the water-rites for their fellow-kinsmen at the Gaṅgā. Kuntī, in a paroxysm of grief, disclosed the truth about Karṇa's birth () to her sons. The Pāṇḍavas grieved, and Yudhishṭhira lamented, hearing that Karṇa was his elder brother (). Yudhishṭhira caused Karṇa's wives, etc., to be brought before him, and with them performed the water-rite in honour of Karṇa (XI, 27).

श्रमण
Śramaṇa = Vishṇu (1000 names).

श्रौतश्रव
Śrautaśrava (metron.) = Śiśupāla: III, 637.

श्राव
