दाशार्ही
Dāśārhī^1 (“daughter of the Dacārha king”) = Vijayā, wife of Bhumanyu: I, 3786 (Vº). 

दाशार्ही
Dāśārhī^2 (“do.”) = Sudevā, wife of Vikuṇṭhana: I, 3789 (Sº).

दाशार्ही
Dāśārhī^3 (“do.”) = Śubhāṅgī, wife of Kuru: I, 3792 (Śº).

दशार्ण
Daśārṇa, pl. (ºāḥ), a people. § 177 (Pāṇḍudigvijaya): I, 113, 4449 (vanquished by Pāṇḍu on his digvijaya).--§ 280 (Bhīmasena): II, 29, 1063 (in the east, vanquished by Bhīmasena on his digvijaya).--§ 285 (Nakula): II, 32, 1189 (in the west, vanquished by Nakula on his digvijaya).-§ 350 (Nalopākhyānap.): III, 69, 2708 (tvam tu jātā mayā dṛshṭā (C. ºtvā) Dºeshu pitur gṛhe, says Sunaṇḍā's mother, daughter of Sudāman, the king of the Daśārṇas, to Damayantī, the daughter of her sister).--§ 549 (Pāṇḍavaprav.): IV, 1, 12; 5, 144 (uttareṇa Dºāṃs te Pañcālān dakshiṇena ca).--§ 573 (Ambopākhyānap.): V, 189, 7420 (ruled by Hiraṇyavarman).--§ 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 348 (in Bhāratavarsha), 350 (do.), 363 (do., only C.; B. has Daśāpārśvaº).--§ 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 51, 2103 (in the army of Duryodhana, followed Droṇa).--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 26, 1162 (rājā Dºānāṃ, fought Bhagadatta).--§ 605 (Karṇap.): VIII, 22, 864 (attacked the Pāñcālas).--§ 785 (Anugītāp.): XIV, 83, 2470 (at the time of Yudhishṭhira's horse-sacrifice the D. were ruled by Citrāṅgada, who was vanquished by Arjuna).

दशार्ण
Daśārṇa (“king of the Daśārṇas”) = Hiraṇyavarman: V, 7493 (pārthive), 7519.

दाशार्ण
Dāśārṇa^1 (do.) = Hiraṇyavarman: V, 7445, 7468.

दाशार्ण
Dāśārṇa^2 (do.) = the king of the Daśārṇas at the time of the great battle. § 585 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 95, 4276 (fought Bhagadatta).

दशार्णाधिपति
Daśārṇādhipati^1 (do.) = Sudāman: III, 2707 (Sº).

दशार्णाधिपति
Daśārṇādhipati^2 (do.) = Hiraṇyavarman: V, 7417 (ºeḥ sutāṃ, married to Śikhaṇḍin), 7425, 7459, 7483, 7498, 7500, 7512.

दशार्णाधिपति
Daśārṇādhipati^3 (do.), the king of the Daśārṇas at the time of the great battle. § 585 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 95, 4255 (among the Pāṇḍava warriors) (), 4271 (attacked Bhagadatta).--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 26, 1164 (attacked Bhagadatta).

दाशार्णक
Dāśārṇaka, adj. (“belonging to the Daśārṇas”). § 280 (Bhīmasena): II, 29, 1063 (ºo rājā Sudharmā).--§ 573 (Ambopākh.): V, 189, 7418 (ºsya nṛpateḥ, i.e. Hiraṇyavarman, Ś. has Daº), 7419 (Hiraṇyavarmeti nṛpo yo 'sau Dºḥ smṛtaḥ), 7428 (ºo rājā, i.e. Hiraṇyavarman); 190, 7454 (do.); 191, †7462 (ºe nṛpatau = do.); 192, 7490 (ºo rājā = do.).

दशार्णनृप
Daśārṇanṛpa (“king of the Daśārṇas”) = Hiraṇyavarman: V, 7503.

दशार्णपति
Daśārṇapati (do.) = Hiraṇyavarman: V, 7464, 7509.

दशार्णराज
Daśārṇarāja (do.) = Hiraṇyavarman: V, 7430.

दाशार्णराज
Dāśārṇarāja (do.) = Hiraṇyavarman: V, 7515.

दाशार्णेश
Dāśārṇeśa (do.), the king of the Daśārṇas at the time of the great battle. § 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 50, 2080 (in the army of Yudhishṭhira).

दाशार्णिक
Dāśārṇika, adj. (“belonging to the Daśārṇas”). § 573 (Ambopākh.): V, 189, 7424 (dhātryaḥ). Cf. Dāśārṇaka.

दशास्य
Daśāsya = Rāvaṇa, q.v.

दशावर
Daśāvara, an Asura. § 268 (Varuṇasabhāv.): III, 9, 367 (among the Daityas and Dānavas in the palace of Varuṇa).

दशेरक
Daśeraka, pl. (ºāḥ), a people. § 589 (Droṇābhishek.): VII, 11, 397 (had formerly been vanquished by Kṛshṇa).--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 20, 798 (in the army of Duryodhana). Cf. next.

दाशेरक
Dāśeraka, pl. (ºāḥ), a people. § 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): 50, 2080 (ºgaṇaiḥ, in the army of Yudhishṭhira).--§ 580 (do.): VI, 56, 2409 (ºgaṇaiḥ, in the army of Duryodhana; C. has Dāsº).--§ 587 (do.): VI, 117, 5483 (ºgaṇāh, attacked Arjuna; C. has Dāsº). Cf. prec.

दाशेयी
Dāśeyī (“daughter of the fisherman”) = Satyavatī: I, 4015; V, 5966 (C. Dāsº).

दशीविदर्भ
Daśīvidarbha, pl. (ºāḥ), a people. § 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 372 (in the south; B. has Ṛshīkā Vidabhāh).

दधीच
Dadhīca, an ancient ṛshi. § 208 (Astradarśana): I, 137, 5430 (Indra's vajra had been made from the bones of D.).-§ 368 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 83, 7057 (ºsya…tīrthaṃ). --§ 378 (do.): III, 92, 8437 (ºa iva Devendraṃ… tathā rakshasva).--§ 384 (Agastyop.): III, 100, 8695 (mahān ṛshiḥ), 8701 (ºsyāśramaṃ), 8706 (ºāśramaṃ), 8707, †8709 (requested by the gods, D. gave up his life, then Tvashṭṛ made the vajra from his bones).--§ 615gg (Sārasvata): IX, 51, 2929 (muniḥ; when D. saw the Apsaras Alambushā his vital seed came out; from that seed Sārasvata was born by the river Sarasvatī), 2952 (the weapons of Indra were made from D.'s bones; (§ 615hh: D. had been begotten by the paramarshi Bhṛgu (son of Prajāpati) by his penances; of stout limbs and great energy, D. was the strongest of the creatures in the world (lokasāraḥ) and became tall as the king of the mountains; Indra had always been afraid of his energy).--§ 717b (Nārāyaṇīya): XII, 343, VII), ††13212 (Bhārgavaḥ), ††13213 (Dhātṛ made the vajra from D.'s bones). Cf. Dadhīci.

दधीचि
Dadhīci = Dadhīca. § 695b (Dakshayajñavināśa): XII, 285, 10283, 10288, (10293), (when Śiva had not been invited to Daksha's sacrifice, D. saw by his power of yoga what would happen, and warned Daksha).--§ 717b (Nārāyaṇīya): XII, 343, 13268 (Dºvacanād Dakshayajñam apāharat, sc. Rudra, all. to § 695b). Cf. Dadhīca.

दधिमुख
Dadhimukha^1, a serpent. § 47 (Sarpanāmak.): I, 35, 1553 (enumeration).--§ 564 (Mātalīyop.): V, 103, 3628 (enumeration).

दधिमुख
Dadhimukha^2, a monkey. § 534 (Setubandhana): III, 283, 16275 (harivṛddhaḥ, came to Rāma with a large army of monkeys).

दधिवाहनपौत्र
Dadhivāhanapautra. § 638b (Rāmopākhy.): XII, 49, 1796 (Dadhivāhanapautras tu putro Divirathasya ca | guptas sa Gautamenāsīd Gaṅgākūle 'bhirakshitaḥ. PCR. connects this śloka with the next (cf. Bṛhadratha^3). According to Harivaṃśa, v. 1693 foll., the grandson of Dadhivāhana and son of Diviratha is a king [of the Aṅgas?]<BR>named Dharmaratha).

दग्धरथ
Dagdharatha = Citraratha^1 (the king of the Gandharvas): I, 6475.

दहदहा
Dahadahā, a mātṛ. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2638.

दहन
Dahana^1, one of the eleven Rudras. § 108 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 66, 2567 (son of Sthāṇu).--§ 191 (Arjuna): I, 123, 4826 (present at the birth of Arjuna).

दहन
Dahana^2 = Agni, q.v.

दहन
Dahana^3, a companion of Skanda. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 45, 2536 (given to Skanda by Aṃśa).

दहति
Dahati, a companion of Skanda. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 45, 2536 (given to Skanda by Aṃśa).

दाहोजतुगृहस्य
Dāho jatugṛhasya. § 10 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 313 (i.e. Jatugṛhaparvan).

दैतेय
Daiteya, pl. (ºāḥ) (“sons or descendants of Diti”), a class of the enemies of the gods (= Daitya, pl.). § 28 (Amṛtamanthana): I, 18, 1157 (Dānava-Dºāḥ, after the churning of the ocean Nārāyaṇa took away the amṛta from them).-§ 130 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2668 (Śarabho nāma yas teshāṃ Dºānāṃ mahāsuraḥ).--§ 320 (Saubhavadhop.): III, 17, 695 (Saubhavāsinaḥ, i.e. the followers of Śālva^5); 19, 766 (ºāstraṃ, employed by Śālva).--§ 334 (Kairātap.): III, 41, 1694 (ebhis--i.e. the nooses of Varuṇa--tadā mayā vīra saṃgrāme Tārakāmaye | Dºānāṃ sahasrāṇi saṃyatāni mahātmanāṃ, says Varuṇa).--§ 358 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 82, 5017 (hatvā Dº-Dānavān, sc. Vishṇu).--§ 378 (do.): III, 94, 8491 (ºā Dānavāś ca), 8497 (ºān Dānavāṃś ca Kalir apy āviśat).--§ 445 (Nivātakavacayuddhap.): III, 173, 12215, 12220, 12223, 12226 (i.e. the inhabitants of Hiraṇyapura).-§ 512 (Ghoshayātrāp.): III, 245, 14996 (dahyamānā …Dºā iva Śakreṇa).--§ 513 (do.): III, 251, 15144 (º-Dānavāḥ, summoned Duryodhana into their presence).--§ 564 (Mātalīyop.): V, 98, 3536 (hṛtarājyānāṃ); 99, 3557 (atra--i.e. in Pātāla--te dharmaniratā baddhāḥ kālena pīḍitāḥ | Dºā nivasanti sma Vāsavena hṛtaśrayaḥ); 105, 3684 (ºvigrahe).--§ 567 (Bhagavadyānap.): V, 128, 4301, 4303, 4304 (Dharma bound the D. and the Dānavas and made them over to Varuṇa, who kept them within the depth of the ocean).--§ 581 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 65, 2965 (ºānāṃ vadhāya ca).--§ 599 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 122, 4910 (petuḥ…devāsure purā yuddhe yathā Dº-Dānavāḥ).--§ 605 (Karṇap.): VIII, 31, 1295 (yathā).--§ 608 (do.): VIII, 73, 3690 (purā Vishṇur iva hatvā Dº-Dānavān).--§ 611 (Śalyap.): IX, 25, 1352 (trailokyavijaye yuktā yathā Dº-Dānavāḥ).--§ 615 (Baladevatīrthay.): IX, 43, †2448 (Dānavānaṃ Dºānāṃ Rākshasānāñ ca devaiḥ…yuddhaṃ Tārakākhyaṃ).-§ 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2685 (sarva-Dºā Rākshasā Dānarāḥ, defeated by the gods commanded by Skanda).-§ 632b (Shoḍaśarāj., cf. § 595, v. Yayāti): XII, 29, 990 (vyūḍhenāsurayuddhena hatvā Dº-Dānavān, sc. Yayāti).-§ 650 (Āpaddh.): XII, 142, 5442 (ºān Uśanāḥ prāha saṃśayacchedanaṃ purā).--§ 671b (Bali-Vāsavas.): XII, 223, 8074 (ºā vyatishṭhaṃs tava--i.e. Bali's--śāsane).-§ 673b (do.): XII, 227, 8266 (Daiteyā Dānavāś caiva, enumeration of ancient rulers of the earth).--§ 674b (ŚrīVāsavas.): XII, 229, 8360 (hitvā Dº-Dānavān, sc. Śrī).-§ 707 (Mokshadh.): XII, 319, 11786.--§ 768 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 148, 6899 (Daiteyā Dānavendrāś ca…cakrāgnau kshayam āpannāḥ). Cf. Asura, pl.; Daitya, pl.; Dānava, pl.; Ditija, pl.

दैतेय
Daiteya, sg. (cf. Daiteya^1). Names of single Daiteyas:-Aśvapati: I, 2651 (Aº). Bāṇa: IX, 2700 (Bº). Śibi: I, 2644 (Śº). Hiraṇyakaśipu: XII, 12942 (Hº). Ilvala: III, 8543 (Iº), 8552 (Iº). Maya: II, 10, 16 (Mº). Prahlāda: XII, 8032 (Pº). Tāraka: XIII, 4012, 4019. Vegavat: III, 675 (Vº). Vipracitti: XII, 3661 (Vº). Virocana: V, 1187 (Vº). Virūpāksha: I, 2658 (Vº). Cf. Asura, sg.; Daitya, sg.; Dānava, sg.

दैतेय
Daiteya, adj. (“belonging to Diti”). § 664 (Mokshadh.): XII, 207, 7544 (ºī prajā).

दैतेयापसद
Daiteyāpasada = Śālva^5: III, 796.

दैतेयी
Daiteyī = Pulomā: III, 12203 (Pº). 

दैत्य
Daitya, pl. (ºāḥ) (“sons of Diti”), a class of the enemies of the gods (= Daiteya, pl.). § 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 369 (ºānāṃ…samudbhavaḥ).--§ 28 (Amṛtamanthana): I, 19, 1158 (º-Dānavāḥ, battled with the gods about the amṛta).--§ 32b (Garuḍa): I, 23, 1247 (ahito Dº-Rakshasāṃ, sc. Garuḍa).--§ 84 (Ādivaṃśāvatāraṇap.): I, 64, 2482 (Ādityaiḥ…nirjitā yudhi).--§ 121 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 66, 2607 (Uśanas became their guru).--§ 146 (Devayānī): I, 78, 3297, 3310 (ºānām asi gāyaneḥ, sc. Uśanas); 80, 3343 (ºendrānāṃ); 81, 3396.--§ 147 (do.): I, 82, 3410 (ºkanyāṃ, i.e. Śārmishṭhā).--§ 190d (Arjuna): I, 123, 4801 (Nivātakavacā nāma Dºāḥ, will be vanquished by Arjuna, cf. § 443 foll.).--§ 233 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 187, †7011 (came to see the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).--§ 246 (Sundopasundop.): I, 209, 7650 (hṛshtaṃ pramuditaṃ sarvaṃ Dºānām abhavat puraṃ), 7651; 210, 7653, 7654 (ºsenayā); 212, 7730 (ºgaṇaḥ).--§ 257 (Khāṇḍavadah.): I, 225, 8198 (armed with the discus Kṛshṇa is superior to the D.).--§ 258 (do.): I, 227, 8259 (ºDānavasaṅghānāṃ cakāra kadanaṃ mahat, sc. Kṛshṇa); 228, 8292 (ºāḥ Kṛshṇacakravidāritāḥ).--§ 268 (Varuṇasabhāv.): II, 9, 368 (ºDānavasaṅghāḥ, in the palace of Varuṇa).--§ 270 (Brahmasabhāv.): II, 11, 472 (come as guests to the palace of Brahmán).--§ 271 (Lokapālas.): II, 12, 480 (ºendrāḥ, in the palace of Varuṇa).--§ 299 (Śiśupālavadhap.): II, 45, 1580 (cakraṃ Dºgarvanisādanam, sc. Kṛshṇa's).-§ 317b (Kṛshṇa Vāsudeva): III, 12, 478 (avadhīs tvaṃ-i.e. Kṛshṇa--raṇe sarvān sametān DºDānavāṇ).--§ 334 (Kairātap.): III, 41, 1669 (accompanied Varuṇa).--§ 345 (Nalopākh.): III, 56, 2170 (ºDānavamardanaṃ Mahendraṃ). --§ 357 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 82, 4065 (had performed austerities in Pushkara and attained to godhood).--§ 378 (do.): III, 94, 8499 (niryaśaskās tathā Dºāḥ kṛtsnaśo vilayaṃ gatāḥ), 8509 (vinaṅkshyanti Daityā iva).--§ 384 (Agastyop.): III, 101, 8729 (ºvare, i.e. Vṛtra); 102, 8744 (i.e. the Kāleyas), [8758 (Ādidaityaḥ… Hiraṇyakaśipuḥ)].--§ 432 (Saugandhikāh.): III, 154, †11390 (sa Śakravad Dānava-Dºsaṅghān vikramya).-§ 443 (Nivātakavacayuddhap.): III, 168, 12074 (sahasrāṇi prayutāny arbudāny api rathenānena Dºānāṃ jitavān Maghavā yudhi).--§ 444 (do.): III, 169, 12085 (ºpuraṃ); 171, 12137 (i.e. the Nivātakavacas); 172, 12162, 12165, 12186 (ºnāryaḥ).--§ 445 (do.): III, 173, 12202 (ºānāṃ puraṃ, i.e. Hiraṇyapura), 12222 (i.e. the inhabitants of Hiraṇyapura).--§ 453 (Mārkaṇḍeyas.): III, 183, 12610.--§ 459 (do.): III, 188, 12925 (seen by Mārkaṇḍeya in the stomach of Nārāyaṇa); 189, 12977 (are slain when born among men, by the incarnate Nārāyaṇa [Vishṇu]).--§ 474b (Dhundhumārop.): III, 201, 13503 (ºendrāḥ parābhūtāḥ, sc. by Vishṇu).--§ 476 (do.): III, 202, 13534 (avadhyo devatānāṃ hi Dºānām atha, etc., sc. Dhundhu).--§ 495 (Skandotpatti): III, 224, 14264 (jetā yo dushṭa-Dºānāṃ). --§ 502 (Manushyagrahak.): III, 230, 14483 (ºānāṃ yā Ditir mātā).--§ 507 (Skandayuddha): III, 231, 14588, 14589, 14595 (ºbalāt), 14603, 14605, 14608 (ºsenā), 14614 (ºgaṇāḥ, battle with the gods).--§ 513 (Ghoshayātrāp.): III, 251, 15150 (summoned Duryodhana into their presence); 252, 15172 (ºRakshogaṇān, re-born as warriors in the great battle), 15177 (re-born as the Saṃśaptakas), 15181.-§ 514 (do.): III, 252, 15198.--§ 522 (Draupadīharaṇap.): III, 265, †15589 (Koṭika believes Draupadī to be a Daityavarāṅganā); 270, †15710 (ºsenāsu).--§ 524d (Vishṇu): III, 272, 15834 (ºānām ādipurushaḥ, i.e. Hiraṇyakaśipu).- § 526 (Rāmopākhyānap.): III, 275, 15927 (ºānāṃ devānāñ ca balotkaṭaḥ ākramya ratnāny aharat, sc. Rāvaṇa).--§ 533 (Sītā-Rāvaṇas.): III, 281, 16175 (ºānāṃ…yoshitaḥ, wives of Rāvaṇa).--§ 542 (Rāvaṇavadha): III, 290, 16510 (º-Dānavān, had been slain by Indra).--§ 547 (Karṇa): III, 310, 17201.--§ 548e (Vishṇu): III, 315, 17461 (vadhārthaṃ Dºānāṃ).--§ 552 (Goharaṇap.): IV, 58, 1887 (jetāraṃ deva--Dºānāṃ, i.e. Arjuna).--§ 554b (Vishṇu): V, 10, 297 (had been slain by Vishṇu).--§ 554 (Indravijaya): V, 14, 445 (ºDānavasūdana, i.e. Indra, C. has by error ºaṃ.).--§ 556 (Sañja