दक्षदुहितृ
Dakshaduhitṛ (“daughter of Daksha”) = Svāhā: III, 14295 (Sº).

दक्षकन्या
Dakshakanyā (do.): Kadrū: I, 2521 (Kº).

दक्षक्रतुहर
Dakshakratuhara (“destroyer of Daksha's sacrifice”): X, 253; XII, 13149; XIII, 6565.

दक्षप्रोक्तशिवसहस्रनामस्तोत्र
Dakshaprokta-Śivasahasranāmastotra (“the 1008 names by which Śiva was praised by Daksha”). § 696b (Mokshadh.): Daksha praised Śiva by enumerating his 1008 names (i.e. Śivasahasranāmastotra), and adding some further praises. Śiva became gratified and granted Daksha some further boons (among those the benefits of the Pāśupata religion); then Śiva disappeared. Blessing to the reader.

दक्षयागापहारिन्
Dakshayāgāpahārin = Śiva (1000 names^2).

दक्षयज्ञनिबर्हण
