द्रौपद
Draupada (“son of Drupada”) = Śikhaṇḍin: VI, 4966 (Śº, only B., C. has by error Drupadaḥ); VIII, †3506 (Śº).

द्रौपदेय
Draupadeya, pl. (ºāḥ) (“sons of Draupadī”), the five sons of the Pāṇḍavas and Draupadī. § 4 (Anukram.): I, 1, 210 (all. to § 616).--§ 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 429 (read with B. nayanaṃ instead of tayanaṃ, all. to § 321), 570 (all. to § 616).--§ 130 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2762 (pañca, incarnations of the Viśvadevagaṇa; their names are: Prativindhya, Sutasoma (C. Sutāº), Śrutakīrti, Śatānīka (Nākuliḥ), and Śrutasena, cf. v. 2451).--§ 253 (Haraṇāharaṇap.): I, 221, 8046 (born with intervals of one year; their names are: Prativindhya (by Yudhishṭhira), Sutasoma (by Bhīmasena), Śrutakarman (by Arjuna), Śatānīka (by Nakula), and Śrutasena (by Sahadeva)).--§ 292 (Rājasūyikap.): II, 45, 1609 (accompanied the Parvatīyas, etc.). --§ 321 (Saubhavadhop.): III, 22, 897 (when the Pāṇḍavas went to the forest, Dhṛshṭadyumna took the D. with him to his capital).--§ 554 (Sainyodyogap.): V, 1, †6 (kumārāḥ). --§ 556 (Sañjayayānap.): V, 22, †684 (pañca).--§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 48, †1839; 50, 2008; 56, †2231 (kumārān); 57, 2251.--§ 569 (Bhagavadyānap.): V, 141, 4737 (pañca), 4743 (do.), 4748 (do.), 4778.--§ 570 (Sainyaniryānap.): V, 151, 5144; 152, 5152.--§ 571 (Ulūkadūtāg.): V, 162, 5592; 164, 5709 (are pitted against the Trigartas).--§ 572 (Rathātirathas.): V, 170, 5879 (pañca, regarded as mahārathas).--§ 573 (Ambopākhyānap.): V, 184, 7629, (), 7635.--§ 576 (Bhagavadgītāp.): VI, 19, 711 (protected Bhīmasena); 25, 835, 847.--§ 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 50, 2068 (), 2082 (in the wings of Yudhishṭhira's array); 51, 2118.--§ 579 (do.): VI, 52, 2150.--§ 580 (do.): VI, 57, 2454.--§ 581 (do.): VI, 62, 2733; 63, 2789.--§ 582 (do.): VI, 69, 3066 (in the back of Yudhishṭhira's array), 3081.--§ 583 (do.): VI, 75, 3283 (in the neck of the Pāṇḍavas' makaravyūha); 77, 3394; 78, 3438 (fought with Duryodhana); 79, 3470.--§ 585 (do.): VI, 87, 3867; 89, 3949; 95, 4254, (), 4271, 4310 (pañca, fought with Bhagadatta).-§ 586 (do.): VI, 100, 4565, 4566 (fought with Alambusha). --§ 587 (do.): VI, 108, 4998; 118, 5554.--§ 589 (Droṇābhishekap.): VII, 8, 228; 10, 356 (proceeded against Droṇa).--§ 590 (do.): VII, 14, 578; 16, 626, 628 (fought with Vṛshasena), (), 646.--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 23, 1035 (description of their standards: pañcānāṃ Dºānāṃ pratimā dhvajabhūshaṇaṃ | Dharma-Māruta-Śakrāṇām Aśvinoś ca mahātmanoḥ), 1041 (enumeration of their bows: Raudram Āgneyaṃ Kauberyaṃ Yāmyaṃ Giriśam eva ca | pañcānāṃ Dºānāṃ dhanūratnāni, Bhārata!); 25, 1095 (fought with Aśvatthāman; PCR. reads Draupadeyaḥ= Prativindhya); 26, 1186.--§ 593 (Abhimanyuvadhap.): VII, 35, 1511; 40, 1691, 1694 (description of their standards: Dharma-Māruta-Śakrāṇām Aśvinoḥ pratimās tathā | dhārayanto dhvajāgreshu Dºāḥ); 43, 1770.--§ 597 (Pratijñāp.): VII, 83, 2951.--§ 598 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 85, 3050:--§ 599 (do.): VII, 95, 3527 (fought with Bālhīka); 96, 3553 (do.); 106, 3979 (fought with Saumadatti, i.e. Bhūriśravas); 108, 4053 (do.); 109, 4111, 4113; 111, 4282; 114, 4502; 124, 5002.-§ 600 (Ghaṭotkacavadhap.): VII, 153, 6628; 154, 6652; 156, 6764; 158, 7013; 177, 8060.--§ 601 (Droṇavadhap.): VII, 184, 8367.--§ 603 (Nārāyaṇāstram.): VII, 197, 9123.--§ 605 (Karṇap.): VIII, 12, 454; 21, 845; 22, 870, (), 888; 30, 1230.--§ 608 (do.): VIII, 46, 2158, 2206 (pañca…Arjunasamāḥ); 47, 2215 (protected Dhṛshṭadyumna); 48, 2253, (), 2280 (), 2286; 49, 2333, (), 2360; 55, 2652, 2661; 56, 2755; 59, 2946; 61, 3079; 66, 3319; 73, 3731; 78, 3955, 3958 (so B., C. has Draupadeyaḥ), 3964, (), 4002; 79, 4029; 93, 4873.--§ 609 (Śalyap.): IX, 1, 32 (lamented for as slain); 2, 79.--§ 610 (do.): IX, 3, 165; 7, 335.--§ 611 (do.): IX, 11, 550, 561, 566, 572; 16, 801; 17, †894; 18, 962, 967, 968; 21, 1126; 22, 1139, 1143, 1164; 23, 1214, 1217, 1242.--§ 612 (Hradapraveśap.): IX, 30, 1726.--§ 615 (Gadāyuddhap.): IX, 62, 3462.--§ 616 (Sauptikap.): X, 8, 366, 371 (slain by Aśvatthāman in the night encounter), 476 (nihatāḥ); 9, 479 (hatvā…Dºān), 529 (hatāḥ).--§ 617 (Aishīkap.): X, 10, 544 (hatāḥ).--§ 618 (Jalaprādānikap.): XI, 11, 300 (pātitāḥ); 12, 321.--§ 620 (Śrāddhap.): XI, 26, 790 (their bodies are cremated); 27, 821 (ºvadhena).--§ 621 (Rājadh.): XII, 1, 15 (ºāṃś ca ghātayitvā).--§ 637 (do.): XII, 42, 1490 (their śrāddha is performed).--§ 788 (Āśramavāsikap.): XV, 21, 588 (ºānāṃ…vadhaṃ saṃsmṛtya).--§ 789 (Putradarśanap.): XV, 32, 875 (among the dead warriors who, summoned by Vyāsa, arose from the Gaṅgā); 33, 892 (do.).--§ 793 (Mausalap.): XVI, 3, 81 (all. to § 616).--§ 795 (Svargārohaṇap.): XVIII, 1, 26; 3, 67, (), 69.

द्रौपदेय
Draupadeya, dual (ºau). § 599 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 147, 6330 (follow Sātyaki; it seems that Yudhāmanyu and Uttamaujas are meant, who possibly were sons or grandsons of Drupada).

द्रौपदेय
Draupadeya^1, sg. § 604 (Karṇap.): VIII, 5, 103 (who?, had slain Dauḥśāsani).

द्रौपदेय
Draupadeya^2 = Śikhaṇḍin(!): VI, 5695 (Śº).

द्रौपदेय
Draupadeya^3 (“son of Draupadī”) = Śrutakarman: VII, 981 (Śº, son of Sahadeva?).

द्रौपदेय
Draupadeya^4 (do.) = Śrutakīrti: VII, 982 (Śº, son of Arjuna?), 1095 (Ārjuniṃ Śrutakīrtiṃ).

द्रौपदेय
Draupadeya^5 = Sutasoma: IX, 502 (Sº).

द्रौपदि
Draupadi (“son of Drupada”) = Dhṛshṭadyumna: VIII, 288.

द्रौपदी
Draupadī, the wife of the Pāṇḍavas (her proper name was Kṛshṇā (K.); as daughter of the Pāñcāla king Drupada she was named Draupadī, Pāñcālī (P.), Pārshatī (Pār.), and Yājñasenī (Y.)).--§ 4 (Anukram.): I, 1, [125 (K.), 148 (K.)], 152, 155, [167 (K.)].--§ 10 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, [314 (P.)].--§ 11 (do.): I, 2, [361 (P.), 384 (K.)], 385, 388, 392, 394, 395, 402 (ºyās tanayān), 413, [427 (P.), 430 (K.)], 452, [456 (P.)], 469, 473, [483 (P.)], 573, 574, 578, 630, 632.--§ 71 (Ādivaṃśāvatāraṇap.): I, 61, [2259 (K.)], 2260 (all. to § 231 foll.).--§ 72 (do.): I, 62, 2289 (Kṛshṇā). --§ 83 (Ādivaṃśāvataraṇa): I, 63, [2438 (K., all to § 218)], 2450 (Pāñcālyāṃ, mother of five sons: Prativindhya from Yudhishṭhira, Sutasoma from Bhīmasena, Śrutakīrti from Arjuna, Śatānīka from Nakula, and Śrutasena from Sahadeva). --§ 132 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2791 (born from a portion of Śacī).--§ 158 (Pūruvaṃś.): I, 95, ††3826 (wife of the Pāṇḍavas, mother of Prativindhya, Sutasoma, Śrutakīrti, Śatānīka, and Śrutakarman).--§ 216 (Caitrarathap.): I, 165, [6322 (Yājñasenyāḥ svayāṃvaraṃ), 6323 (ayonijatvaṃ Kṛshṇāyā Drupadasya mahāmakhe, all. to § 218), 6325 (vedīmadhyāc ca Kṛshṇāyāḥ sambhavaḥ, all. to § 218)], 6327 (ºsambhavaṃ).--[§ 218 (Draupadīsambhava): I, 167, 6398 (P.), 6402 (K.), 6407 (origin of the name Kṛshṇā: kṛshṇā bhūtā hi varṇataḥ; D. arose from the centre of the vedī at the sacrifice of Drupada).]--[§ 220 (Caitrarathap.): I, 169, 6434 (K., Pār., in a former existence D. five times had asked Śiva for a husband, therefore she was destined to become the wife of the five Pāṇḍavas).]--[§ 230 (Dhaumyapurohitak.): I, 183, 6920 (P.), 6924 (Pāñcālyās taṃ svayaṃvaraṃ).]--§§ 231--236 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 184, 6925, 6934, [6942 (K.)]; 185, [6952 (K.)], 6974, [6977 (K.). †6979 (K.)]; 187, [†7007 (K.), †7008 (Drupadātmajāṃ), †7009 (K. Drupadātmajārthaṃ), †7015 (K.)], †7016, [†7024 (K.)], †7027; [188, †7059 (K.)]; 189, 7062; [190, 7123 (P.), 7125 (K.)]; 191, [†7131 (Y.), †7132 (K.), †7133 (Y.), 7141 (P.),