दुःशलोत्पत्ति
[Duḥśalotpatti(ḥ)]<BR>(“birth of Duḥśalā”). § 181 (Sambhavap.): That Gāndhārī also had a daughter (Duḥśalā) was due to the circumstance that Vyāsa, when he divided the lump of flesh (knowing that Gāndhārī wished to have a daughter), assigned one part in excess of the hundred to become a daughter (I, 116).

