गर्ग
Garga, a ṛshi. § 615e (Gargasrotas): IX, 37, 2132 (atra-i.e. in Gargasrotas--Gºena vṛddhena…kālajñānagatiś caiva jyotishāṃ vyatikramaḥ | utpātā dāruṇāś caiva śubhāś ca), 2135. --§ 615ii (Vṛddhakanyā): IX, 52, 2981 (Kuṇiḥ), 2982 (do.).--§ 641f (Pṛthu Vainya): XII, 59, 2232 (the astrologer (sāṃvatsaraḥ) of Pṛthu Vainya).--§ 707 (Mokshadh.): XII, 319, 11783 (had instructed Viśvāvasu).--§ 730 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 18, (1334) (Śiva bestowed on G., who gratified him on the bank of Sarasvatī, the knowledge of time with its sixty-four branches (catuḥshashṭyaṅgaṃ…kālajñānaṃ) and 1000 sons; through the grace of Śiva the lifetime of G. and his sons became extended to ten millions of years).

