Gautama^1 (“descendant of Gotama”), name of one or more ṛshis. § 22 (Pramadvarā): I, 8, 962 (came to see the dead Pramadvarā).--§ 170 (Dīrghatamas): I, 104, 4194 (the eldest son of Dīrghatamas and Pradveshī), 4205 (with his brothers he threw Dīrghatamas into the Gaṅgā).--§ 191 (Arjuna): I, 123, 4807 (among the seven ṛshis, present at the birth of Arjuna).--§ 264 (Sabhākriyāp.): II, 4, 112 (among the munis who were present when Yudhishṭhira entered his palace).--§ 266 (Śakrasabhāv.): II, 7, 298 (Kākshīvān?, in the palace of Indra).--§ 270 (Brahmasabhāv.): II, 11, 436 (in the palace of Brahmán).--§ 275 (Rājasūyārambhap.): II, 17, 698 (Kākshīvataḥ).--§ 277 (Jarāsandhavadhap.): II, 21, 802 (near Rājagṛha G. begat, with the śudrā Auśīnarī, the sons Kākshīva, etc.), 803, 804, 805.-§ 370 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 84, 8086 (Brahmarsher Gºsya vanaṃ, a tīrtha).--§ 376 (do.): III, 85, 8263 (among the ṛshis who expected Yudhishṭhira on his tīrthayātrā).--§ 455 (Brāhmamāhātmyak.): III, 185, 12684, 12685, (12691), 12692, (12693), 12698, 12699.--§ 545 (Pativratāmāhātmyap.): III, 298, (16868), (16890).--§ 602 (Droṇavadhap.): VII, 190, 8727.--§ 615b (Udapāna): IX, 36, 2073 (father of Ekata, Dvita, and Trita).--§ 637 (Rājadh.): XII, 47, 1597 (among the ṛshis who surrounded Bhīshma).--§ 638b (Rāmopākhyāna): XII, 49, 1796 (Dadhivāhanapautras tu putro Divirathasya ca | guptas sa Gºenāsīd Gaṅgākūle 'bhirakshitaḥ).--§ 641 (Rājadh.): XII, 129, 4718 (ºsya ca saṃvādaṃ Yamasya ca), 4719, 4721, (4724).--§ 656 (Khaḍgotpatti): XII, 166, 6142.--§ 658b (Kṛtaghnop.): XII, 168, 6298, 6300, 6301, 6302, 6305, 6307; 169, 6317, 6327, 6331, 6332, 6333, 6339; 170, 6342, 6346, 6348, 6350, 6351, 6358, 6362, 6363, 6366; 171 ((6372), 6394, 6396, 6398; 172, 6412, 6415, 6417; 173, 6439, 6441, 6442, 6445 (the story of the ingratitude of G.).--§ 665 (Mokshadh.): XII, 208, 7699 (one of the ṛshis of the north).--§ 672b (Śakra-Namucisaṃv.): XII, 226, †8206 (not in the text of B., but mentioned by Nīl. as varia lectio, according to Nīl. the husband of Ahalyā).--§ 682 (Mokshadh.): XII, 267, 9484 (father of Cirakārin), 9488, 9525 (Medhātithiḥ), 9539, 9541, 9546, 9548 (when Indra had violated the wife of G. (i.e. Ahalyā, Nīl.), he commanded his son Cirakārin to slay her. Cirakārin hesitated to do so, and G. meanwhile repented that he had given the order).-§ 707 (do.): XII, 319, 11783 (had instructed Viśvāvasu).-§ 717b (Nārāyaṇīya): XII, 343, II), ††13205 (the husband of Ahalyā whom Indra violated; G. then cursed Indra to wear a green beard).--§ 730 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 17, 1289 (Śukra communicated the 1000 names of Śiva to G.), 1290 (G. again communicated them to Manu Vaivasvata).--§ 733 (do.): XIII, 25, 1691 (questioned Aṅgiras about the tīrthas), 1755.--§ 734 (do.): XIII, 26, 1761 (among the ṛshis who surrounded Bhīshma).--§ 743b (Vipulop.): XIII, 41, 2328 (ºenāsi yan mukto bhagāṅgaparicihnitaḥ (bhagāṅkaº, B.), sc. Indra; “that Gautama had cursed thee, in consequence of which thy body became disfigured with a thousand sex-marks, which, by the Ṛshi's mercy, were afterwards changed into organs of vision,” PCR.).--§ 746 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 66, 3320 (maharshiḥ, ascended to heaven by making gifts of sesame seeds).--§ 750b (Bisastainyop.): XIII, 93, 4416, (), (4442), (), (4467), (), (4490), 4491 (etymology, B. has Gotamaṃ), (), (4523).--§ 751b (Śapathavidhi): XIII, 94, 4550, (), 4565.--§ 757b (Hastikūṭa): XIII, 102, 4845 (ºsya munes tāta saṃvādaṃ Vāsavasya ca), 4846, 4849, (†4854), †4855, (†4856), (†4858), (†4860), (†4862), (†4865), (†4867), (†4871), (†4874), (†4877), (†4880), (†4882), (†4884), 4891, (†4896), (†4899), (†4901), 4904, 4905.--§ 759 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 106, 5200.--§ 770 (do.): XIII, 151, 7116 (one of the ṛshis of the north).--§ 772e (Pavanārjunasaṃv.): Indra coveting Ahalyā was cursed by Gautama, but, for the sake of righteousness, he was not hurt (hiṃsitaḥ): XIII, 154, 7218. --§ 775 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 166, 7668 (one of the ṛshis of the west).--§ 782g (Guruśishyasaṃv.): X