Janamejaya^10, Pārikshit. § 652b (Indrota-Pārīkshitīya): XII, 150, 5595, 5596 (Pārīkshit, B. has Pāriº), 5600; 151, 5613, (5627), (5634); 152, 5638, 5642, 5673 (J. had slain a brahman, but was instructed by Indrota Śaunaka about the means of cleansing himself; Indrota then assisted J. in his horse-sacrifice. J. here belongs to the past (cf. also Harivaṃśa, vv. 1608 ff.), but seems originally to be identical with Janamejaya^1 (Pārikshita)).

