Karṇātmaja^2 (do.) = Satyasandha: VIII, †210 (Sº).

कर्णात्मज
Karṇātmaja^3 (do.) = Susheṇa: VIII, †3816. Cf. Karṇaputra.

कर्णात्मज
Karṇātmaja^4 (do.) = Prasena: VIII, †4183 (Pº). Cf. Karṇaputra.

कर्णवेष्ट
Karṇaveshṭa, a prince. § 130 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2696 (among the incarnations from the Krodhavaśa gaṇa).--§ 554 (Sainyodyogap.): V, 4, 78 (among the princes to whom the Pāṇḍavas ought to send messengers).

कार्णि
Kārṇi (“the son of Karṇa”) = Vṛshasena: VIII, †4302. Cf. Karṇaputra, Karṇasuta, Karṇātmaja.

कर्णिका
Karṇikā, an Apsaras. § 191 (Arjuna): I, 123, 4820 (among the Apsarases who sang at the birth of Arjuna).

कर्णिकारध्वज
Karṇikāradhvaja (“having a Karṇikāra flower in his banner”) = Abhimanyu: VI, 5365 (Saubhadraṃ).

कर्णिकारमहास्रग्विन्
Karṇikāramahāsragvin = Śiva (1000 names^2).

कर्णिकारस्रजप्रिय
Karṇikārasrajapriya = Śiva (1000 names^1).

करोटक
Karoṭaka, a serpent. § 47 (Sarpanāmak.): I, 35, 1553 (enumeration).

कर्पट
Karpaṭa, v. Pañcakarpaṭa.

कार्ष्ण
Kārshṇa, adj. (“composed by Kṛshṇa, i.e. Vyāsa”). § 7 (Anukram.): I, 1, 261 (ºṃ vedaṃ, i.e. the Mahābhārata).-§ 72 (Ādivaṃśāvatāraṇap.): I, 62, 2300 (do.).--§ 795 (Svargārohaṇap.): XVIII, 5, 188 (do.).

