कृष्ण
Kṛshṇa^2 = Vyāsa: I, 60, 614 (ṛsheḥ), †2103 (Satyavatyāḥ sutasya), 2220 (pitāmahāya), 2324, 4234, 4365, 7252, 7254; II, 1633, 2573 (Dvaipāyanena); VII, 8881 (Satyavatyāḥ sutasya); IX, 3531 (pitāmahaḥ), 3538; XI, 429 (maharsheḥ); XII, 12182, 12573; XIII, 421 (? so Nīl.), 1338, 5797, 5798; XIV, 355 (Dvaipāyanena), 1875 (Vyāsaḥ), 2659 (Dvaipāyanaḥ); XVIII, 183.

कृष्ण
Kṛshṇa^3, a serpent. § 268 (Varuṇasabhāv.): II, 9, 360 (among the serpents in the palace of Varuṇa).

कृष्ण
Kṛshṇa^4 = Arjuna Pāṇḍava: II, 1814 (? so PCR.); IV, 1376 (enumeration of the ten names of Arjuna), 1378, 1389 (etymology); XIV, 2228.

कृष्ण
Kṛshṇa^5, a mountain. § 575 (Bhūmip.): VI, 12, 445 (in the western dvīpa, dear to Nārāyaṇa).

कृष्ण
Kṛshṇa^6, a warrior of Skanda. § 615u (Skanda); IX, 45, 2559.

कृष्ण
Kṛshṇa^7, a ṛshi. § 637 (Rājadh.): XII, 47, 1599 (among the ṛshis who surrounded Bhīshma on his arrow-bed).

कृष्ण
Kṛshṇa^8 = Śiva: XII, 10409 (1000 names^1); XIII, 1158 (1000 names^2); XIV, 203.

कृष्ण
