[91, 3236 (P.)].-§ 567 (do.): V, 132, (4463) (told Kṛshṇa to urge Yudhishṭhira to battle).--§ 568 (Vidulāputraśāsana): V, 133, (4494); 136, (4637) (asked Kṛshṇa to tell Yudhishṭhira Vidulāputraśāsana).--§ 569 (do.): V, 137, (4644), 4645 (sent Kṛshṇa with a message to the Pāṇḍavas); 138, 4676, 4677; 140, 4753; 141, 4758, 4775 (ºyāḥ prathamajaṃ, i.e. Karṇa); 144, [4885 (P.)], 4894, 4910, [4912 (P.)], [4914 (Kauravyapatnī Vārshṇeyī)], 4915, 4916; 145, (4918); 146, [4930 (P.)], 4952, [4955 (P.)]<BR>(Kṛshṇa told Karṇa that he was the son of K., Kuntī disclosed to Karṇa that she is his mother and solicited him to make peace with the Pāṇḍavas, Karṇa promised to save the Pāṇḍavas except Arjuna).--§ 570 (Sainyaniryāṇap.): V, 154, 5219, 5239.--§ 583 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 79, 3453 (ºyāḥ parikleśaṃ).--§ 588 (do.): VI, 122, 5841 (avakīrṇas tv ahaṃ Kºyā, says Karṇa).- § 599 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 127, 5166; 131, 5364, 5377 (ºyāḥ putrasya sadṛśaṃ nedaṃ); 132, 5425 (saputrāṃ, all. to § 213); 139, 5783 (ºyā vacaḥ smaran, sc. Karṇa, cf. § 569).--§ 600 (Ghaṭotkacavadhap.): VII, 167, 7481 (ºyāḥ smṛtvā vacāḥ, sc. Karṇa, cf. § 569).--§ 605 (Karṇap.): VIII, 24, 964 (smṛtvā Kºyā vacaḥ, sc. Karṇa, cf. § 569).--§ 608 (do.): VIII, 49, 2352 (ºvākyañ ca so 'smarat, sc. Karṇa, cf. § 569); 68, [†3382 (Pṛthāyā garbhaṃ), †3389 (read Pṛthāṃ with B.)], †3393 (a celestial voice came to K. at the birth of Arjuna); [†3400 (garbhe…Pṛthāyāḥ)]; 69, †3433; 70, †3528; 87, 4488.--§ 613 (Gadāyuddhap.): IX, 33, 1903 (Pāṇḍoḥ Kºyāś ca santatiḥ).--§ 618 (Jalapradānikap.): XI, 10, 270, 272 (came to see the battle-field); 14, 374 (yathā); [15, 414 (P.), 415 (P.), 419 (P.)].--§ 620 (Śrāddhap.): XI, 27, 805 (disclosed to the Pāṇḍavas that Karṇa was her son).--§ 621 (Rājadh.): XII, I, 18, 21 (gūḍhotpannaḥ sutaḥ Kºyāḥ, i.e. Karṇa), 22, 24 (jyeshṭhaputraḥ Kºyāḥ, sc. Karṇa), [26 (P.), 27 (P.), 31 (P.), 35 (P.), 36 (P.), 38 (P.)], 42 (Pṛthāyāḥ); 4, 139 (ºyāś ca varadānena, Karṇa was slain on account of the boon he had g