कुन्तिभोज
Kuntibhoja (“the king of the Kuntis (and the Bhojas?)”), name of the adoptive father of Kuntī, and of the [adoptive]<BR>brother of Kuntī (= Purujit(?)). § 131 (Kuntī): I, 67, 2766 (cousin of Śūra, who gave him his daughter Pṛthā (afterwards named Kuntī) as a daughter).--§ 175 (Karṇasambhava): I, 111, 4383 (repetition of § 131).--§ 176 (Kuntīvivāha): I, 112, 4412 (duhitā Kºsya Pṛthā, i.e. Kuntī), 4414, 4420 (ºsya duhitrā, i.e. Kuntī), 4421.--§ 281 (Sahadeva): II, 31, 1110 (in the south, vanquished by Sahadeva on his digvijaya).-§ 287 (Rājasūyikap.): II, 34, 1271 (came to the rājasūya of Yudhishṭhira).--§ 547 (Karṇa): III, 303, 17001, 17003, 17006; 304, 17039; 305, 17057, 17067 (C. by error ºtībhº) (K., the adoptive father of Kuntī, ordered her to wait upon a brahman).--§ 562 (Bhagavadyānap.): V, 90, 3191, 3192 (Kuntī was given to K. by Śūra).--§ 569 (do.): V, 141, 4781 (mātulaḥ Bhīmasenasya, among the allies of Yudhishṭhira); 144, 4904 ([adoptive]<BR>father of Kuntī).--§ 570 (Sainyaṇiryāṇap.): V, 151, 5163 (sided with Yudhishṭhira).--§ 572 (Rathātirathasaṅkhyānap.): V, 172, 5922 (mātulo Bhīmasenasya, in B. his name is Purujit (? = C. ripujit); among the atirathas in Yudhishṭhira's army).--§ 576 (Bhagavadgītap.): VI, 25, 834 (in Yudhishṭhira's army).--§ 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 45^21, 1740, 1742, 1743 (K. and his son fought with Vinda and Anuvinda); 50, 2079 (K. and Śaibya in the eye section of Dhṛshṭadyumna's krauñcavyūha).--§ 583 (do.): VI, 75, 3287 (K. and Śatānīka in the foot section of Dhṛshṭadyumna's makaravyūha).--§ 585 (do.): VI, 89, 3948.-§ 586 (do.): VI, 99, 4511.--§ 587 (do.): VI, 110, 5098; 118, 5554.--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 23, 995 (Purujit (C. purajit) mātulaḥ Savyasācinaḥ, description of his horses).--§ 593 (Abhimanyuvadhap.): VII, 35, 1508.-§ 599 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 95, 3537 (fought with Alambusha); 96, 3559, 3560 (do.); 111, 4284.--§ 600 (Ghaṭotkacavadhap.): VII, 156, 6912 (ºsutān, ten of K.'s sons are slain by Aśvatthāman); 157, 6922 (ºsutān… nihatān).--§ 604 (Karṇap.): VIII, 6, 172 (Purujit Kºaś ca mātulau (!) Savyasācinaḥ, slain by Droṇa; read mātulaḥ?).-§ 609 (Śalyap.): IX, 2, 79. Cf. Kunti, Kuntirāja, Purujit.

