Mahendra^2, a mountain, the abode of Rāma Jāmadagnya. § 84 (Ādivaṃśāvatāraṇap.): I, 64, 2459 (parvatottame).-§ 201 (Droṇa): I, 130, 5120, 5121.--§ 249 (Arjunavanavāsap.): I, 215, 7824 (ºparvataṃ, visited by Arjuna Pāṇḍava).--§ 252 (Subhadrāharaṇap.): I, 219, 7907 (only C., but read with B. mahe tasya instead of Mahendrasya).--§ 269 (Vaiśravaṇasabhāv.): II, 10, 412 (present in the palace of Kubera).--§ 370 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 85, 8158 (Jāmadagnyanishevitaṃ).-§ 377 (Dhaumyatīrthak.): III, 87, 8318 (ºo nāma Bhārgavasya, in the east).--§ 378 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 93, 8467 (ºādīṃś ca parvatān).--§ 383 (Paraśurāma): III, 99, 8681.--§ 392 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 114, †10124 (visited by Yudhishṭhira, etc., on their tīrthayātrā).--§ 398 (Paraśurāma): III, 117, 10209 (śailendre).--§ 399 (Mahendrācalagamana): III, 117, 10213.--§ 459 (Mārkaṇḍeyas.): III, 188, 12919 (seen by Mārkaṇḍeya in the stomach of Nārāyaṇa).--§ 573 (Ambopākhyānap.): V, 176, 6054; 186, 7338.--§ 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 318 (among the kulaparvatāḥ of Bhāratavarsha).-§ 595 (Shoḍaśarāj., v. Rāma Jāmadagnya): VII, 70, 2447 (parvatottamaṃ, having given the earth to Kaśyapa, Rāma took his abode on M.).--§ 621 (Rājadh.): XII, 2, 59 (parvataṃ), 62 (svargasammite).--§ 775 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 166, 7657 (enumeration).--§ 782g (Guruśishyasaṃv.): XIV, 43, 1174 (do.).

महेन्द्र
Mahendra^3 = Rāvaṇa(?): II, 410 (Rākshasādhipatiḥ, but the text seems to be in disorder, cf. v. 412).

