Mainda, a monkey king. § 281 (Sahadeva): II, 31, 1122 (vānararājābhyāṃ Mºena Dvividhena ca, at Kishkindhā, vanquished by Sahadeva on his digvijaya).--§ 531 (Rāmopākhyānap.): III, 280, 16115 (ºaś ca Dvividhaś cāpi, among the counsellors of Sugrīva).--§ 535 (Setubandhana): III, 283, 16287 (ºMº-Dvividhaº, in the army of Sugrīva). --§ 541 (Indrajidvadha): III, 289, 16468 (SusheṇaMº-Dvividhaiḥ, do.) (), 16477 (Mº-Dvividha-Nīlāḥ).-§ 542 (Rāvaṇavadha): III, 290, 16500.

