Mānasa^2, a sacred lake, the present Manasarovara (or Mansaraur). § 279 (Arjuna): II, 28, 1041 (sara uttamaṃ, in. the region Hāṭaka), 1042 (saraḥ).--§ 410 (Plakshāvataraṇag.): III, 130, 10547 (ºsya dvāraṃ).--§ 587 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 119, 5665 (haṃsāḥ…Mºaukasaḥ).--§ 607 (Haṃsakākīyop.): VIII, 41, 1894 (do.).--§ 608 (Karṇap.): VIII, 60, 3048 (ºād etya haṃsair Gaṅgeva).--§ 652b (Indrota-Pārīkshitīya): XII, 152, 5647 (PCR. is hardly right in connecting Mānasaḥ saraḥ with Sarasvatī-Dṛshadvatyoḥ saṅgamaḥ).--§ 717b (Nārāyaṇīya): XII, 343, VII), ††13213 (ºsarogatāṃ nalinīṃ), ††13215 (saraḥ).--§ 772l (Vasishṭha): XIII, 156, 7280 (saraḥ, only B., C. has Vaikhānasaṃ). Cf. Mānasa(ṃ) tīrtha(ṃ), Uttaramānasa

