मन्दार
Mandāra (so. B.; Mandara, C.), son of Hiraṇyakaśipu. § 730c (Hiraṇyakaśipu): M. succeeded, through the boon he had obtained from Śiva, in fighting Indra for a million of years; neither the thunderbolt of Indra nor the discus of Vishṇu could make the slightest impression in his body: XIII, 14, 663.

