नर
Nara, pl. (ºāḥ), a class of Gandharvas. § 269 (Vaiśravaṇasabhāv.): II, 10, 396 (in the palace of Kubera).

नारद
Nārada^1, a Devarshi, son of Parameshṭhin, often mentioned together with Gandharvas and therefore presumably himself a Gandharva. Cf. Nārada^2. § 4 (Anukram.): I, 1, 106 (recited the Mahābhārata to the gods); †172 (vadato Nºsya, all. to § 561d).--§ 5 (do.): I, 1, 221, 223bis (surarshiṇā, enumerated to Śaibya (Śvaitya, B.), twenty-four kings who have died).--§ 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 394, 408, 440 (maharshiṇā), 462 (surarshiṇā), 616.--§ 59 (Sarpasattra): I, 53, 2048 (ºaḥ Parvatas tathā, among the sadasyas at the snake sacrifice of Janamejaya).--§ 138 (Daksha Prācetasa): I, 75, 3132 (taught the sons of Daksha sāṅkhyajñānaṃ).-§ 221 (Caitrarathap.): I, 170, 6497 (ºprabhṛtīnāṃ-devarshīṇāṃ).--§ 233 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 187, †7011 (Viśvāvasur Nº-Parvatau, present at the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).-§ 245 (Rājyalābhap.): I, 208, 7604 (devarshiḥ), 7608, 7610, (7612).--§ 246 (Sundopasundop.): I, 209, (7619), (7644); 210, (7652); 211, (7679), (7700); 212, (7711), (7736), 7739, 7740 (devarshiḥ), 7741, 7742 (N. related to Yudhishṭhira the Sundopasundepākhyāna and caused the Pāṇḍavas to establish a rule among themselves with regard to Draupadī).--§ 250 (Arjunavanavāsap.): I, 217, 7874 (devarshiṃ, directed Vargā, etc., to go to Nārītīrthāni and prophesied their deliverance by Arjuna).--§ 265 (Lokapālasabhākhyānap.): II, 5, 144, 147 (ṛshiṃ), (151), (247), 248 (muniḥ), (249), 261, (263) (questioned Yudhishṭhira about his government); 6, 269, 273, (274), 278, 282.--§ 266--70 (do.): II, 7, (283); 8, (311); 9, (353); 10, (383); 11, (420) (described the different sabhās of the gods).--§ 271 (do.): II, 12, (488) (told Yudhishṭhira that Pāṇḍu wished that he should perform a rājasūya), 512, 513.--§ 289 (Arghāharaṇap.): II, 36, 1308 (maharshayaḥ…Nºpramukhāḥ), 1315, 1316, 1318, 1325 (knew that Kṛshṇa was Nārāyaṇa); 39, 1407 (praised Kṛshṇa).--§ 293 (Dyūtap.): II, 46, 1635 (a saying of his about the rājasūya is quoted).--§ 296 (do.): II, 53, 1917 (at the rājasūya N. sprinkled water over Yudhishṭhira). --§ 305 (Anudyūtap.): II, 78, 2575 (would become the instructor of Yudhishṭhira).--§ 306 (do.): II, 80, 2652 (foretold the great battle).--§ 310b (Sūrya): III, 3, 209 (learnt the hymn to the Sun from Śakra and taught it to Dhaumya).--§ 317b (Kṛshṇa Vāsudeva): III, 12, 500 (had told Arjuna about the nature of Kṛshṇa), 513 (a saying of his about Kṛshṇa is quoted).--§ 320 (Saubhavadhop.): III, 19, 770 (the gods sent N. and the Wind as messengers to Kṛshṇa).--§ 322 (Dvaitāvanapraveśa): III, 24, 924 (wanders over all the worlds, waited upon Yudhishṭhira).--§ 324 (do.): III, 26, 985 (waited upon Yudhishṭhira).--§ 327 (Draupadīparitāpav.): III, 31, 1171.--§ 336 (Indralokābhigamanap.): III, 43, 1769 (Tumburur Nºś-caiva, in the abode of Indra).--§ 345 (Nalopākhyānap.): III, 54, 2117 (ºḥ Parvataś caiva), 2119, 2120, 2123, 2128 (told Indra about the svayaṃvara of Damayantī).--§ 348 (do.): III, 66, 2612 (maharshiḥ, had cursed Karkoṭaka).--§ 356 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 81, 4022 (devarshiṃ), 4026 (ṛshiḥ), (4032) (repeated the description of tīrthas delivered by Pulastya to Bhīshma).--§ 364 (do.): III, 83, 6051 (ºsya…tīrthaṃ…Ambājanma), 6052.--§ 376 (do.): III, 85, (8255), 8274 (ṛshiḥ, having completed the description of tīrthas, N. disappeared).-§ 377 (Dhaumyatīrthak.): III, 86, 8276, 8280 (knew Kṛshṇa and Arjuna to be Nārāyaṇa and Nara); 88, 8347 (devarshiṇā, a śloka of his about Ujjayanta is cited).-§ 378 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 93, 8470 (all. to § 356 foll.), 8475 (Parvata-Nºau, came to Yudhishṭhira), 8483.--§ 387 (Sagara): III, 107, 8882 (informed Sagara of the death of his sons).--§ 412 (Ashṭāvakrīya): III, 134, †10659 (dvau devarshī Nº-Parvatau).--§ 447 (Nivātakavacayuddhap.): III, 175, 12308 (sent by the gods to prevent Arjuna from discharging the celestial weapons).--§ 453 (Mārkaṇḍeyas.): III, 183, 12603 (devarshiḥ, came to Yudhishṭhira), 12605 (do.).--§ 463 (Śibi): III, 194, ††13249, ††13249 bis, ††13250 (quoted three ślokas in order to settle the dispute between Śibi an