Nārītīrthāni, pl., name of five tīrthas. § 250 (Arjunavanavāsap.): I, 217, 7871 (i.e. Agastyatīrtha, Saubhadra, Pauloma, Kārandhama, and Bhāradvājasya tīrthaṃ (v. 7841 foll.), assigned by Nārada to five Apsarases (Vargā, etc.), who had been cursed to become crocodiles; at his visit at N. Arjuna liberated the Apsarases from the curse).--§ 400 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 118, †10217 (visited by Yudhishṭhira, etc.; all. to § 250).

