पितामहसरस्
Pitāmahasaras (“the lake of the Grandsire”), name of one or more tīrthas. § 370 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 84, 8126 (near Śailarāja [i.e. Himavat]).--§ 377 (Dhaumyatīrthak.): III, 89, 8369 (= Pushkara). Cf. next.

पितामहस्यसरस्
Pitāmahasya saras (do.), name of one or more tīrthas. § 370 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 84, 8127 (thence comes the Kumāradhārā).--§ 615q (Sarasvatī): IX, 42, 2387 (thence comes the Sarasvatī; = Mānasa, PCR.). Cf. the prec. 

पितामहसुत
Pitāmahasuta^1 (“the son of Pitāmaha [i.e. Brahmán]”) = Atri: XIII, 3289 (Aº).

पितामहसुत
Pitāmahasuta^2 (do.) = Sanatkumara: IX, 2716 (Sº); XII, 1355 (Kumāraṃ).

पिता
Pitā, mātā, pitāmaha(ḥ) = Sūrya (the Sun): III, 156.

पीतात्मन्
Pītātman = Śiva (1000 names^2).

पीतवासस्
Pītavāsas = Kṛshṇa, q.v.

पीतवासिनी
Pītavāsinī = Durgā (Umā): VI, 800.

पीठ
Pīṭha, an Asura. § 589 (Droṇābhishekap.): VII, 11, 386 (had been slain by Kṛshṇa).--§ 717b (Nārāyaṇīya): XII, 340, 12956 (Dānavaṃ, will be slain by Kṛshṇa, in a prophecy).

पिठर
Piṭhara, an Asura. § 268 (Varuṇasabhāv.): II, 9, 366 (in the palace of Varuṇa).

