Pulkasa, v. Pukkaśa.

पुलोमा
Pulomā^1, the wife of Bhṛgu. § 20 (cf. Paulomap.): P., the wife of Bhṛgu, had first been betrothed to the Rākshasa Puloman, who one day when Bhṛgu was absent came to carry her away, and asked the sacrificial fire whether she was rightly his or Bhṛgu's wife. The Fire (Agni) answered that she was Bhṛgu's, by whom she had been taken with holy rites and invocations (I, 5). When Puloman began to carry her away Cyavana dropped from her womb, and Puloman instantly was converted to ashes. Of her tears Brahmán formed the river Vadhūsarā, Bhṛgu cursed Agni (b) (I, 6--7): I, 5, 875, 876, 879, 893, 894; 6, 900, 905, (908), 910.--§ 565 (Gālavacarita): V, 117, 3971 (reme…yathā Bhṛguḥ Pºyāṃ).

पुलोमा
Pulomā^2, a female Asura. § 445 (Nivātakavacayuddhap.): III, 173, 12203 (Daiteyī, obtained boons from Brahmán for her offspring, the great Asuras, viz. the Paulomas).

पुलोमन्
Puloman, a Rākshasa, or Asura. § 20 (Pulomā): I, 5, 877 (rakshaḥ), 881 (carried-away Pulomā, but was burnt to ashes, when she in her terror gave birth to Cyavana); 7, 938. --§ 92 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 65, 2530 (fourth son of Danu).-§ 673b (Bali-Vāsavas.): XII, 227, 8262 (among the ancient rulers of the earth). Cf. Dānava, Dānavanandana, Rakshas.

पुंस्
Puṃs = Śiva (1000 names^1).

पुनश्चन्द्रा
Punaścandrā: § 377 (Dhaumyatīrthak.): III, 88, 8338 (a vedī in Śūrpāraka, belonging to Jamadagni).

पुनरावर्तनन्दा
Punarāvartanandā, name of a tīrtha. § 733u (Ānuśāsanik.): By bathing in P., as also in Mahānandā, one attains to Nandana. By bathing in the tīrtha Urvaśī on the river Lohitya on the day of full moon of the month of Kārttika one obtains the merits of a puṇḍarīka sacrifice: XIII, 25, 1731.

पुनर्वसु
Punarvasu^1, name of a nakshatra (v. Sū. Si.). § 608 (Karṇap.): VIII, 49, 2328 (rathābhyāse cakāśete candrasyeva Pºḥ, B. Pºvasū, dual).--§ 746 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 64, 3260 (merit of making gifts under the constellation of P.).-§ 749 (do.): XIII, 89, 4258 (merit of performing a śrāddha under the constellation of P.).--§ 759 (do.): XIII, 110, 5392 (description of the cāndravrata).

पुनर्वसु
Punarvasu^2 = Kṛshṇa (Vishṇu): XII, 1511; XIII, 6965 (Vishṇu's 1000 names).

पुण्डरीक
Puṇḍarīka^1, an ancient king. § 267 (Yamasabhāv.): II, 8, 325 (in the palace of Yama).

पुण्डरीक
Puṇḍarīka^2, a tīrtha. § 364 (Tīrthāyātrāp.): III, 83, 6053.

पुण्डरीक
Puṇḍarīka^3, a serpent. § 564 (Mātalīyop.): V, 103, 3622 (enumeration).--§ 793 (Mausalap.): XVI, 4, †119.

