Purujit^2, a Kunti prince. [P. seems in the most passages (except only VIII, 172) to be another name of Kuntibhoja.]<BR>--§ 273 (Rājasūyārambhap.): II, 14, 581 (mātulo bhavataḥ (i.e. Yudhishṭhira's) …Pºt Kuntivardhanaḥ).--§ 572 (Rathātirathas.): V, 172, 5922 (Pºt (so B., C. ripujit) Kuntibhojaś ca…mātulo Bhīmasenasya).--§ 576 (Bhagavadgītāp.): VI, 25, 834 (Pºt Kuntibhojaś ca).--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 23, 995 (Kuntibhojaḥ… Pºt (C. Puraº) mātulaḥ Savyasācinaḥ, description of his horses); 25, 1103 (fought with Durmukha).--§ 604 (Karṇap.): VIII, 6, 172 (Pºt Kuntibhojaś ca mātulau Savyasācinaḥ | sangrāmanirjitān lokān gamitau Droṇasāyakaiḥ).--Cf. Kuntibhoja, Kuntivardhana^1.

