Rucirāṅgada = Vishṇu (1000 names).

रुद्र
Rudra, pl. (ºāḥ), a class of gods, followers of Śiva (Rudra). § 44 (Garuḍa): I, 30, 1416.--§ 46 (do.): I, 32, 1486.-§ 106 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 65, 2562 (ºāṇāṃ, sc. sambhavaḥ).-§ 108 (do.): I, 66, 2567 (eleven sons of Sthāṇu, viz. Mṛgavyādha, Sarpa, Nirṛti, Ajaikapād, Ahirbudhnya, Pinākin, Dahana, Īśvara, Kapālin, Sthāṇu, Bhaga).--§ 120 bis (do.): I, 66, 2602 (ºāṇāṃ pakshaḥ).--§ 130 (do.): I, 67, 2712 (ºāṇāṃ gaṇāt, Kṛpa was born from the R.).--§ 191 (Arjuna): I, 123, 4826 (present at the birth of Arjuna, their names as in § 108).--§ 233 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 187, 7010 (ºādityāḥ, present at the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).--§ 238 (Pañcendrop.): I, 197, †7277, †7315.--§ 258 (Khāṇḍavadahanap.): I, 227, 8269 (fought with Kṛshṇa and Arjuna).--§ 270 (Brahmasabhāv.): II, 11, 460 (in the palace of Brahmán).--§ 309 (Āraṇyakap.): III, 2, 127.--§ 310b (Sūrya): III, 3, 174 (worship the Sun), 190 (Sūrya identified with the R.).-§ 330 (Indradarśanap.): III, 37, 1490.--§ 331 (Kairātap.): III, 39, 1590 (sg., = Śiva?).--§ 336 (Indralokābhigamanap.): III, 43, 1768.--§ 338 (do.): III, 46, 1840.-§ 347 (Nalopākhyānap.): III, 62, 2356.--§ 357 (Pushkara): III, 82, 4064 (in Pushkara).--§ 359 (Vaḍavā): III, 82, 5037 (worshipped Kṛshṇa at Vaḍavā).--§ 360 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 82, 5063 (? in Rudrakoṭi Śiva had multiplied himself into a koṭi of forms--koṭīti Rºāṇāṃ--for the sake of the munis).--§ 370 (do.): III, 84, 8102 (adore Janārdana at sthānaṃ Nārāyaṇasya).--§ 383 (Paraśu-Rāma): III, 99, 8673 (seen in the body of Rāma Dāśarathi, the incarnate Vishṇu).--§ 412 (Ashṭāvakrīya): III, 134, †10668 (eleven in number).--§ 443 (Nivātakavacayuddhap.): III, 168, 12043.--§ 459 (Mārkaṇḍeyas.): III, 188, 12924 (seen in the body of Nārāyaṇa).--§ 506 (Skandayuddha): III, 231, 14549.--§ 512 (Ghoshayātrāp.): III, 237, 14782 (ºair iva Yamaḥ (sic!), sc. vṛtaḥ).--§ 547 (Karṇa): III, 308, 17139. --§ 548 (Āraṇeyap.): III, 313, 17317; 314, 17421.-§ 549c (Arjuna): IV, 2, 48 (dvādaśaṃ Rºāṇāṃ, sc. Arjuna). --§ 556 (Sañjayayānap.): V, 29, †823 (ºādityāḥ).--§ 562 (Bhagavadyānap.): V, 86, 3043 (yathā).--§ 567 (do.): V, 128, 4301; 131, 4420.--§ 572 (Rathātirathasaṅkhyānap.): V, 169, 5865 (ºvat).--§ 576 (Bhagavadgītāp.): VI, 34, 1227 (ºāṇāṃ Śaṅkaraś cāsmi, says Kṛshṇa); 35, 1252 (seen in Kṛshṇa), †1268 (do.).--§ 589 (Droṇābhishekap.): VII, 6, 159 (ºāṇām iva Kāpālī, sc. senāpatiḥ).--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 23, 1007 (Samudrasenaputraṃ Rºtejasaṃ, sg.?); 35, 1536 (Sādhya-Rº-Marutkalpaiḥ).--§ 596 (Pratijñāp.): VII, 76, 2682 (in Arjuna's oath).--§ 605 (Karṇap.): VIII, 15, 597 (ºau dvāv iva).--§ 608 (do.): VIII, 87, 4418 (sided with Arjuna).--§ 615u (Skanda): IX, 44, 2479 (ºādityāḥ); 45, 2508 (came to the investiture of Skanda), 2555 (made gifts to Skanda).--§ 615ff (Asita Devala): IX, 50, 2893 (ºāṇāṃ…sthāṇaṃ).--§ 626 (Rājadh.): XII, 21, 634.--§ 641 (do.): XII, 64, 2395 (observe kshatriya duties); 122, 4498 (ºāṇām api ceśānaṃ-i.e. Śiva--goptāraṃ), 4502 (īśvaraḥ…sarveshām eva Rºāṇāṃ Śūlapāṇiḥ, i.e. Śiva).--§ 656 (Khaḍgotpattik.): XII, 166, 6141.--§ 661 (Mokshadh.): XII, 198, 7192 (ºāditya-Vasūnāṃ, sc. sthānāni).--§ 664 (do.): XII, 207, 7540 (sons of Dharma?).--[§ 665 (do.): XII, 208, 7585 foll. (The names here enumerated, viz. Ajaikapād, Ahirbradhna, Virūpāksha, Raivata, Hara, Bahurūpa, Tryambaka, Sureśvara, Sāvitra, Jayanta, Pinākin, seem to be quoted in order to give a list of the Rudras.)]--§ 673b (BaliVāsavasaṃv.): XII, 227, 8220 (accompanied Indra), 8288 (had been vanquished by Bali).--§ 695b (Dakshayajñavināśa): XII, 285, 10279 (present at Daksha's sacrifice), 10292 (śūlahastāḥ kapardinaḥ | ekādaśasthānagatāḥ).--§ 696b (Dakshaprokta--Śivasahasranāmastotra): XII, 285, 10456 (description).--§ 702 (Mokshadh.): XII, 296, 10837.-§ 712 (Śukotpatti): XII, 324, 12175.--§ 717b (Nārāyaṇīya): XII, 340, 12915 (ekādaśa), 341, 13043 (ekādaśaite Rºās tu vikārāḥ purushāḥ smṛtāḥ), 13044, 13110 (ºāṇāṃ pataye, sc. Vishṇu).--§ 730g (Upamanyu): XIII, 14, 731 (ºādityāśvināṃ), 910 (ºāṇāṃ Nīlalohitaḥ, sc. Śiva). --§ 730 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 14, 984 (ekādaśa śatāni, surround Śiva); 17, 1141 (ºāṇām api yo Rudraḥ, i.e. Śiva), 1288 (learnt the 1000 names of Śiva from Mṛtyu and communicated them to Taṇḍi(n)); 18, †1368.--§ 747b (Suvarṇotpatti): XIII, 84, 4011; 85, 4131 (together with the Ādityas the R. sprung from the flames of Agni).--§ 759 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 107, 5257 (ºāṇāṃ tam adhīvāsaṃ), (), 5331 (ºāṇāṃ lokaṃ).--§ 766 (do.): XIII, 134, 6186. --§ 770 (do.): XIII, 151, 7091 (ekādaśa, their names are the following: Ajaikapād, Ahirbradhna, Pinākin, Ṛta, Pitṛrūpa, Tryambaka, Maheśvara, Vṛshākapi, Śambhu, Havana, and Īśvara).--§ 773b (Kṛshṇa Vāsudeva): XIII, 159, 7387 (ºādityāḥ).--§ 775 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 166, 7642.--§ 778f (Muñjavat): XIV, 8, 183 (worship Śiva on Muñjavat).--§ 784b (Uttaṅka): XIV, 54, 1564.--§ 793 (Mausalap.): XVI, 4, 129 (ºādityāḥ, received Kṛshṇa in heaven).--§ 795 (Svargārohaṇap.): XVIII, 3, 88.

रुद्र
Rudra^2 = Śiva, q.v.--Do.^3 = Sūrya: III, 148.--Do.^4 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

रुद्रगर्भ
Rudragarbha = Agni, q.v.

रुद्रज
Rudraja (“born from Rudra”) = Aśvatthāman: XV, 858 (Drauṇiṃ).

रुद्रकोटि
Rudrakoṭi, name of two tīrthas. § 360 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 82, 5060, 5066.--§ 364 (do.): III, 83, 6047.

रुद्रलोक
Rudraloka (“the world of the Rudras or of Rudra [i.e. Śiva]”). § 368 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 83, 7050 (by bathing in Sthāṇuvaṭa one attains to R.).--§ 603 (Nārāyaṇāstramokshap.): VII, 202, 9641 (one attains to R. by hearing the Śatarudriya).--§ 759 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 107, 5304.

रुद्रमार्ग
Rudramārga, name of a tīrtha. § 368 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 83, 7052 (only B., C. has Indramārgaṃ).

रुद्रपद
Rudra(ṃ) pada(ṃ), name of a tīrtha. § 360 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 82, 5042 (PCR. Raudrapada).

रुद्राणी
Rudrāṇī = Umā, q.v.

रुद्रपत्नी
Rudrapatnī (“the wife of Rudra (Śiva)”) = Umā: III, 7041.

रुद्ररोमा
Rudraromā, a mātṛ. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2625.

रुद्रसेन
Rudrasena, a Pāṇḍava warrior. § 600 (Ghaṭotkacavadhap.): VII, 158, 7009.

रुद्रास्त्र
Rudrāstra (“the weapon of Rudra (Śiva)”). § 616 (Sauptikap.): X, 8, 352 (Aśvatthāman slew the Pāñcālas with the R.).

रुद्रसूनु
Rudrasūnu (“the son of Rudra (Śiva)”) = Skanda: III, 14428, 14430, 14431, 14432.

रुद्रस्यतीर्थं
Rudrasya tīrthaṃ (“the tīrtha of Rudra”). § 360 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 82, 5047 (Kāmākhyaṃ).

रुद्रात्मन्
Rudrātman = Kṛshṇa: XII, 1669.

रुद्रावर्त
Rudrāvarta, name of a tīrtha. § 370 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 84, 8015.

रुद्रवट
Rudravaṭa, name of a tīrtha. § 358 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 82, 4092 (only C., B. has Bhadravaṭaṃ).

रुक्म
Rukma, a prince. § 233 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 188, †7051. Cf. the foll.

रुक्माङ्गद
Rukmāṅgada, a prince. § 232 (Svayaṃvarap.); I, 186, 6994 (son of Śalya(?), present at the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).--§ 599 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 116, 4610 (fought with Sātyaki).

रुक्मरथ
Rukmaratha^1, son of Śalya. § 232 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 186, 6994 (? present at the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).-§ 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 47, 1857 (only B., C. has. Śvetarathaṃ), 1858 (fought with Śveta).--§ 593 (Abhimanyuvadhap.): VII, 45, 1811 (Madreśvarasutaḥ), 1816 (putraṃ Śalyasya, slain by Abhimanyu).--§ 604 (Karṇap.): VIII, 5, 116 (Śalyaputraḥ, had been slain by Sahadeva).

रुक्मरथ
Rukmaratha^2 (“having a golden chariot”) = Droṇa: IV, 1824; VII, 253, 256, 268, [279], 283, 488, 496, 4675, 8901, 8911; VIII, 94 (Dº).--Do.^3 (do.) = Suśarman: IV, 1059; VII, 4554(?).--Do.^4 (do.) = Virāṭa: V, †784.

रुक्मरथ
Rukmaratha, pl. (ºāḥ), a host of Kuru warriors. § 599 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 112, 4310 (mahārathāḥ, commanded by Karṇa).

रुक्मवाहन
Rukmavāhana (“having a golden chariot”) = Droṇa: VII, 8943.

रुक्मिन्
Rukmin, king of Bhojakaṭa, son of Bhīshmaka, and brother of Rukmiṇī. § 130 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2698 (incarnation of the Krodhavaśa gaṇa).--§ 284 (Sahadeva): II, 31, 1168 (rājñe Bhojakaṭasya, Sahadeva caused R. to pay tribute to Yudhishṭhira).--§ 289 (Arghāharaṇap.): II, 37, 1351.-§ 290 (Śiśupālavadhap.): II, 44, 1536 (purushottamaṃ). --§ 317b (Kṛshṇa Vāsudeva): III, 12, 490 (avāpsīr mahishīṃ Bhojyāṃ--i.e. Rukmiṇī--raṇe nirjitya Rºaṃ, sc. Kṛshṇa, cf. § 570d).--§ 515 (Karṇadigvijaya): III, 254, 15247 (Dākshiṇātyeshu), 15248, 15250 (vanquished by Karṇa on his digvijaya).--§ 554 (Sainyodyogap.): V, 4, 79 (among the princes to whom the Pāṇḍavas ought to send messengers). --§ 561g (Sahadeva): V, 50, 1999 (equal to Sahadeva in strength).--§ 570d (cf. Sainyaniryāṇap.): R. was a disciple of Druma, that lion among the Kimpurushas on the mountain of Gandhamādana. He had obtained from his preceptor the whole fourfold (catushpādaṃ) Dhanurveda and the celestial bow Vijaya, belonging to the great Indra, and equal to the Gāṇḍīva (e) and the Śārṅga (f). When he obtained Vijaya from Druma, R. came to the Pāṇḍavas. Formerly when Kṛshṇa had ravished his sister Rukmiṇī, he set out in pursuit having sworn that he would not return without having slain Kṛshṇa. But he was vanquished and did not return to [his city]<BR>Kuṇḍina; on the spot where he was vanquished he built the city of Bhojakaṭa: V, 158, 5351 (Āhukānām adhipatiḥ Bhojasya yaśasvinaḥ | Dākshiṇātyapateḥ sutaḥ), 5356, 5359.--§ 570 (Sainyaniryāṇap.): V, 158, 5385, 5388 (rejected by Arjuna and by Duryodhana he did not take part in the battle).--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 23, 1017 (astraiḥ samatvaṃ samprāpya Rº--Karnārjunācyutaiḥ, sc. the Pāṇḍya king Sāraṅgadhvaja).--§ 621 (Rājadh.): XII, 4, 113 (came to the svayaṃvara of the daughter of the Kaliṅga king Citrāṅgada).

रुक्मिणी
Rukmiṇī, sister of Rukmin, wife of Kṛshṇa, and mother of Pradyumna, etc. § 132 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2790 (Bhīshmakasya kule, incarnation of a portion of Śrī).--§ 262 (Bhagavadyāna): II, 2, 57.--§ 291 (Śiśupālavadhap.): II, 45, 1574, 1577 (ravished by Kṛshṇa, although she had been intended for Śiśupāla).--§ 317 (Arjunābhigamanap.): III, 12, 575 (yathā tvayā jitā, Kṛshṇa, Rºī Bhīshmakātmajā). --§ 410 (Plakshāvataraṇag.): III, 130, 10554 (āśramaś caiva Rºyāḥ, the same?).--§ 521 (Draupadīharaṇap.): III, 263, 15538 (pārśvasthāṃ śayane tyaktvā Rºṃ Keśavaḥ).-§ 561c (Kṛshṇa Vāsudeva): V, 48, †1881 (yo Rºṃ ekarathena Bhojān utsādya rājñaḥ samare prasahya | uvāha bhāryāṃ yaśasā jvalantīṃ yasyāṃ jajñe Raukmiṇeyo (i.e. Pradyumna) mahātmā, sc. Kṛshṇa).--§ 565 (Gālavacarita): V, 117, 3976 (reme… yathā…Rºyāṃ Janārdanaḥ).--§ 570d (Rukmin): V, 158, 5360 (ºyā haraṇaṃ, ravished by Kṛshṇa).--§ 617b (Brahmaśiras): X, 12, 636 (ºyāṃ yo anvajāyata…Pradyumnaḥ).- § 727 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 11, 508 (discourse between R. and Śrī).--§ 730 (do.): XIII, 14, 617 (PradyumnaCārudeshṇādīn…Rºyāḥ putrakān), 620, 622 (enumeration of R.'s sons with Kṛshṇa).--§ 768 (do.): XIII, 148, 6889 (mother of Pradyumna).--§ 773c (Durvāsas): XIII, 160, 7429, 7434, 7445 (gratified Durvāsas).--§ 793 (Mausalap.): XVI, 5, 145; 7, 249 (when the corpse of Kṛshṇa was burnt, R., etc., ascended the funeral pyre). Cf. Bhīshmakātmajā, Bhojyā.

रुक्मिणिनन्दन
Rukmiṇinandana = Pradyumna, q.v.

रुमण्वत्
