समा
Samā (ºāḥ, pl. C.), a region. § 575c (Bhūmip.): After these regions is seen a habitation of the name Samā. It is of a starry shape with four corners and thirty-three maṇḍalas. There dwell the four world-elephants (diggajāḥ), Vāmana, Airāvata, etc., and also Supratīka, whose dimensions have for ever remained unascertained; there winds blow from all directions and are seized by the elephants with the tips of their trunks and let out over the earth; in consequence thereof people draw breath and live: VI, 12, 473 (ºā nāma dṛśyate (C. ºante) lokasaṃsthitiḥ (C. ºte)).

