Sanatkumāra, a ṛshi, son of Brahmán. § 132 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2786 (incarnate as Pradyumna).--§ 140 (Purūravas): I, 75, 3146 (came from Brahmaloka to give Purūravas counsel which was rejected).--§ 270 (Brahmasabhāv.): II, 11, 441 (yogācāryaḥ, in the palace of Brahmán).--§ 367 (Pṛthūdaka): III, 83, 7017 (had praised the tīrtha Pṛthūdaka).--§ 373 (Prayāga): III, 85, 8213 (ºpramukhāḥ …paramarshayaḥ, in Prayāga).--§ 377 (Dhaumyatīrthak.): III, 90, 8393 (praises Gaṅgādvāra).--§ 413 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 135, 10697 (had obtained success on the Gaṅgā).-§ 455 (Brāhmaṇamāhātmyak.): III, 185, 12700 (12702) (instructed some munis).--§ 581 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 68, 3046 (ºpramukhaiḥ, praise Hari, i.e. Kṛshṇa).--§ 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2716 (Pitāmahasutaṃ prabhuṃ Sºṃ sarveshāṃ Brahmayoniṃ tam agrajaṃ, by some identified with Skanda).--§ 617b (Brahmaśiras): X, 12, 636 (incarnate as Pradyumna).--§ 637 (Rājadh.): XII, 47, 1595 (among the ṛshis who surrounded Bhīshma).--§ 692 (Mokshadh.): XII, 281, 10027 (mahāmuniḥ), 10030, 10086 (discourse with Vṛtra about emancipation and Vishṇu).--§ 694b (Jvarotpatti): XII, 284, 10217 (ºpramukhāḥ…maharshayaḥ).--§ 707 (Mokshadh.): XII, 319, 11784 (had instructed Viśvāvasu).--§ 715 (Śuka-Nāradasaṃv.): XII, 330, 12426 (a saying of his quoted).--§ 717b (Nārāyaṇīya); XII, 340, 12901 (ºtvaṃ labhet, sc. Pradyumna (= manas)); 341, 13078 (the fifth of the mind-born sons of Brahmán); 343, 13200 (ºgīlāḥ ślokāḥ, some ślokas of his are quoted); 349, V), 13587 (studied the religion [of Nārāyaṇa]<BR>and communicated it to Vīraṇa).--§ 730g (Upamanyu): XIII, 14, 916 (ºo yoginām asi, sc. Śiva).--§ 730 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 14, 990.--§ 749 (do.): XIII, 88, 4250 (gāthāḥ …Sºo mayyapi abhāshate, some verses sung by him are quoted).--§ 768b (Kṛshṇa Vāsudeva): XIII, 147, 6850 (ºpramukhāḥ, sc. ṛshayaḥ).--§ 795 (Svargārohaṇap.): XVIII, 5, 160 (after death Pradyumna entered S.). Cf. Brahmayoni, Kumāra, Pitāmahasuta.

सनात्सनातनतम
Sanāt sanātanatama(ḥ) = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सनत्सुजात
Sanatsujāta, a ṛshi. § 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 504 (cf. § 560).--§ 560 (Sanatsujātap.): V, 41, 1566 (kumāro vai yaḥ purāṇah sanātanaḥ); 42, †1578, (†1579), (†1593), (†1595); (†1598), (1602), 43, (†1622), (†1624), (†1627), (1632), 1634, (1635), (1663); 44, †1684, (†1685), (†1687), (†1689), (†1709); 45, (1715), 46, (1737) (instructed Dhṛtarāshṭra).--§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 47, 1791 (all. to § 560): § 717b (Nārāyaṇīya): XII, 341, 13078 (the second of the mind-born sons of Brahmán).

सानत्सुजात
Sānatsujāta, adj. (“relating to Sanatsujāta”). § 10 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 330 (parva Sºṃ, i.e. Sanatsujātaparvan).

सनत्सुजातपर्वन्
[Sanatsujātaparvan(ºva)]<BR>(“the section relating to Sanatsujāta,” the 60th of the minor parvans of the Mhbhr.; cf. Sānatsujāta). § 560: As Dhṛtarāshṭra wished to hear more, Vidura, as he was born in the Śūdra order, did not venture to say more himself, but he thought of that ancient and eternal Ṛshi who, leading a life of perpetual celibacy, had said that there is no death. The Ṛshi came (V, 41), was questioned by Dhṛtarāshṭra, and discoursed upon death, the efficacy of religious acts, etc. (V, 42--46).

सञ्चारक
Sañcāraka, a warrior of Skanda. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 45, 2576.

सण्ड
Saṇḍa, pl. (ºāḥ), a people. § 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 351 (only B., Ć. has Shaṇḍāḥ).

सन्धातृ
Sandhātṛ^1 = Śiva (1000 names^1).--Do.^2 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सन्धिमत्
Sandhimat = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सन्धिपर्वन्
Sandhiparvan = Kṛshṇa: XII, 1634.

सन्ध्या
Sandhyā^1, a river. § 268 (Varuṇasabhāv.): II, 9, 375 (present in the palace of Varuṇa).

सन्ध्या
Sandhyā^2 (“twilight,” personif.). § 565 (Gālavacarita): V, 117, 3970 (wife of Pulastya).

सन्ध्याराग
Sandhyārāga = Śiva (1000 names^1).

साङ्गरेवस्
Sāṅgarevas (I, 2046), v. Śārṅgarava.

सङ्ग्रह
Saṅgraha^1, a companion of Skanda. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 45, 2552 (given to Skanda by the Ocean).--Do.^2 = Śiva (1000 names^2).--Do.^3 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सङ्ग्रहाध्याय
Saṅgrahādhyāya(ḥ) (“outline chapter”) = Parvasaṅgraha: § 4 (Anukram.): I, 1, 88 (ºbījaḥ, sc. Bhāratadrumaḥ).

सङ्ग्रामजित्
Saṅgrāmajit^1, a prince. § 264 (Sabhākriyāp.): II, 4, 116 (waited upon Yudhishṭhira).

सङ्ग्रामजित्
Saṅgrāmajit^2, brother of Karṇa. § 552 (Goharaṇap.): IV, 54, 1666, 1678 (slain by Arjuna).

सनीय
Sanīya, pl. (ºāḥ), a people. § 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 371 (in the south, only C., B. has Sanīpāḥ).

