Sātvata^5 (C. often Sāttº) = Sātyaki: II, 50 (so PCR.); VI, †2592, †2593, 4058 (only C., B. has Sātyakasya), 4694 (Sº), 5387; VII, 343, 1110, 3006, 3608, 3624, 4050, 4142, 4174, 4227, 4238, 4378, 4391, 4420, 4456, 4471, 4480, 4558, 4562, 4567, 4586, 4593, 4595, 4600, 4614, 4635, 4642, 4649, 4658, 4680, 4751, 4788, 4811, 4839, 4876, 4964, 5016, 5107, 5111, 5118, 5119, 5120, 5136, 5138, 5143, 5151, 5168, 5279, 5311(?), 5317(?), 5459 (sa-Sºān), 5868, 5879, 5887, 5926, 5939, 5941, 5978, 6045 (na ca śakyo raṇe jetuṃ Sºo manujarshabhaiḥ), 6094, 6115, 6328, 6332, 6365, 6386, 6496, 6628, 6730, 6732, 6735, 6755, 6784, 6926, 6927, 6930, 6933, 6998 (saha-Sºān), 7001 (sa-Sºān), 7228, 7243, 7247, 7248, 7256, 7281, 7405, 7406, 7639, 7651, 7676, 7681, 7837, 8290, 8653, 8657, 8663, 8807, 8811, 9150, 9169, 9307, 9323; VIII, 518, 2983(?); IX, 124 (ºau i.e. Sātyaki and Kṛshṇa), 351, 787, †1092, 1102 (ºau, i.e. Sātyaki and Kṛtavarman), 1116.

सात्वतश्रेष्ठ
Sātvataśreshṭha^1 = Kṛshṇa: VI, 4865.--Do.^2 = Sātyaki: VII, 5945.

सात्वताग्र्य
Sātvatāgrya = Sātyaki: VI, 780.

सात्वतांपतिः
Sātvatāṃ patiḥ = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सात्वतमुख्य
Sātvatamukhya^1 = Kṛshṇa: II, 1686.--Do.^2 = Pradyumna: III, 754.--Do.^3 = Sātyaki: VII, †4691 (C. Sāttº).

सात्वतप्रवर
Sātvatapravara^1 = Kṛshṇa: II, 1626 (Kº),--Do.^2 = Sātyaki: VII, 5937 (C. Sāttº).

सात्वतपुङ्गव
Sātvatapuṅgava = Sātyaki: VII, 5924 (C. Sāttº).

सात्वतर्षभ
Sātvatarshabha = Sātyaki: VII, 6330 (C. Sāttº).

सात्वतात्मजा
Sātvatātmajā = Subhadrā: I, 7978.

सात्वती
Sātvatī = Subhadrā: I, 8028 (C. Sāttº); XIV, 2020; XV, 23, 348, 437, 778.

सात्वतीपुत्र
Sātvatīputra^1 = Abhimanyu: VI, 3228; VII, 1665, 2573.

सात्वतीपुत्र
Sātvatīputra^2 = Kṛshṇa: II, 1376.

सात्वतीसुत
Sātvatīsuta = Śiśupāla: II, 1566.

सत्वावृहत्त्वा
Satvāvṛhattvā: I, 4813 (so C., B. reads ṛtvābṛhattvā, the text is presumably corrupted, one or two names [of Devagandharvas]<BR>are expected here (perhaps Satvan (or Ṛtvan) and Bṛhatvan); cf. I, 2554, where is read Siddhaḥ Pūrṇaś ca).

सत्य
Satya^1, name of one or more brahmans. § 264 (Subhākriyāp.): II, 4, 105 (waited upon Yudhishṭhira).--§ 686 (Mokshadh.): XII, 273, 9816, 9819, 9823.--§ 736b (Vītahavyop.): XIII, 30, 2001 (son of Vitatya and father of Santa).

सत्य
Satya^2, name of a fire. § 490 (Āṅgirasa): III, 219, 14142 (= Nishkṛti, son of the fire Niścyavana).

सत्य
Satya^3, a Kuru warrior. § 579 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 54^12, 2309 (a Kaliṅga?, slain by Bhīmasena).

सत्य
Satya^4 = Śiva: VII, 2877.--Do.^5 = Kṛshṇa (Vishṇu): XII, 1507, 1614; XIII, 6961 (Vishṇu's 1000 names), 6972 (do.), 7042 (do.).

सत्य
Satya(ṃ) = Śiva (1000 names^1).

सत्या
Satyā^1 = Satyavatī^1: I, 4287, 4292.

सत्या
Satyā^2 = Satyabhāmā: III, 14658, 14706, 14708, †14711, †14716, 14723; V, 2329; XVI, 145 (Sātrājitī).

सत्या
Satyā^3, wife of the fire Śaṃyu. § 490 (Āṅgirasa): III, 219, 14133.

सत्यभामा
Satyabhāmā, daughter of Satrājit, wife of Kṛshṇa Vāsudeva. § 10 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 324 (samvādas tataḥ parva DraupadīSºyoḥ, i.e. Draupadī-Satyabhāmāsaṃv.).--§ 11 (do.): I, 2, 469 (Draupadyāḥ…saṃvādaḥ Sºayā, do.).--§ 452 (Mārkaṇḍeyas.): III, 183, 12563 (sahitaḥ Sºayā, sc. Kṛshṇa), 12567.--§ 453 (do.): III, 183, 12602.--§ 510 (Draupadī-Satyabhāmasaṃv.): III, 233, 14649, 14651, 14657, 14666 (conversation between Draupadī and Satyabhāmā).--§ 511 (do.): III, 235, 14724, 14739 (do.).--§ 549 (Pāṇḍavapraveśap.): IV, 9, 262 (Kṛshṇasya mahishīṃ priyāṃ).-§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 59, 2326.--§ 793 (Mausalap.): XVI, 3, 80; 7, 250 (after the death of Kṛshṇa, S., etc. entered the forest). Cf. Sātrājitī, Satyā.

सत्यश्रवस्
Satyaśravas, a Kuru warrior. § 572 (Rathātirathasaṅkhyānap.): V, 167, 5790 (bṛhadbalaḥ, a ratha in the army of Duryodhana, Nīl. takes satyaśravāḥ as an adj. and Bṛhadbala as the name, but Bṛhadbala is mentioned v. 5765). --§ 593 (Abhimanyuvadhap.): VII, 45, 1805, 1806 (seized by Abhimanyu).

सत्यदेव
Satyadeva, a Kuru warrior. § 579 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 54^12, 2309 (a Kaliṅga(?), slain by Bhīmasena).

सत्यधर्मन्
Satyadharman^1, a Pāñcāla prince. § 569 (Bhaga vadyānap.): V, 141, 4779 (Saumakiḥ, PCR. takes satyadharmā as an adj. to Saumakiḥ = Yudhāmanyu).

सत्यधर्मन्
Satyadharman^2 = Vishṇu (1000 names). Satyadharmaparākrama, Satyadharmaparāyaṇa = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सत्यधृति
Satyadhṛti, one or more princes. § 232 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 186, 6990 (present at the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).-§ 572 (Rathātirathasaṅkhyānap.): V, 171, 5910 (among the mahārathas of the Pāṇḍavas).--§ 573 (Ambopākhyānap.): V, 196, 7649 (Saucittiḥ, in the army of Yudhishṭhira).-§ 585 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 93, 4151 (Saucittiḥ); 95, 4254.--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 23, 988, 990 (Saucittiḥ).--§ 604 (Karṇap.): VIII, 6, 181 (has been slain), 184.

सत्यजित्
Satyajit, a Pāñcāla, son of Drupada. § 209 (Drupadaśāsana): I, 138, 5480, 5483, 5485, 5487, 5488, 5491 (took part in the battle when Droṇa, etc., assailed Drupada).--§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 57, 2235 (ºpramukhaiḥ, sc. the sons of Drupada).--§ 572 (Rathātirathasaṅkhyānap.): V, 171, 5903 (among the Pāñcālas in the army of Yudhishṭhira), 5916 (Drupadātmajaḥ).--§ 591 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 17, 716, 717 (protected Yudhishṭhira).--§ 592 (do.): VII, 21, 858, 860, 865, 867, 870, 871, 875 (do., slain by Droṇa).-§ 603 (Nārāyaṇāstramokshap.): VII, 199, 9228 (yena, i.e. by Droṇa, Pāñcālāḥ Sºmukhāḥ…vinipātitāḥ).--§ 604 (Karṇap.): VIII, 6, 154 (had been slain by Droṇa).--§ 795 (Svargārohaṇap.): XVIII, 5, 149. Cf. Pāñcāla, Pāñcālya.

सत्यक
Satyaka, a Vṛshṇi, son of Śini and father of Sātyaki (Yuyudhāna). § 83 (Ādivaṃśāvatāraṇa): I, 63, 2434 (father of Sātyaki).--§ 252 (Subhadrāharaṇap.): I, 219, 7916 (Sºaḥ Sātyakiś caiva).--§ 253 (Haraṇāharaṇap.): I, 221, 7991 (do.).--§ 264 (Sabhākriyāp.): II, 4, 125 (Śineḥ sutaḥ).--§ 785 (Anugītap.): XIV, 62, 1855. Cf. Śineḥ suta(ḥ) (II, 125).

सात्यक
Sātyaka = Sātyaki, q.v.

सत्यकर्मन्
Satyakarman^1, a Trigarta prince. § 591 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 17, 689 (among five Trigarta brothers who belonged to the Saṃśaptakas).--§ 611 (Śalyap.): IX, 27, 1480 (slain by Arjuna).

सत्यकर्मन्
Satyakarman^2 = Kṛshṇa: XII, 1614.

सात्यकि
Sātyaki (“the son of Satyaka”), a Vṛshni, properly named Yuyudhāna, son of Satyaka and grandson of Śini. [§ 4 (Anukram.): I, 1, †194 (Yuyudhānaṃ)].--§ 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 534, 571.--§ 83 (Ādivaṃśāvatāraṇa): I, 63, 2433 (Sºḥ Kṛtavarmā ca Nārāyaṇam anuvratau, son of Satyaka). = § 130 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2714 (Vṛshṇikulodvahaḥ, born from the paksha of the Maruts).--§ 232 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 186, 6998 (present at the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).-§ 243 (Vidurāgamanap.): I, 205, 7507 (partisan of the Pāṇḍavas).--§ 252 (Subhadrāharaṇap.): I, 219, 7916.-§ 253 (Haraṇāharaṇap.): I, 221, 7991 (came to the wedding of Arjuna and Subhadrā).--§ 264 (Sabhākriyāp.): II, 4, 129 (Yuyudhānaḥ, instructed by-Arjuna in the science of arms).-§ 273 (Rājasūyārambhap.): II, 14, 621 (among the seven atirathas of the Vṛshṇis).--§ 296 (Dyūtap.): II, 53, 1920 (held the umbrella for Yudhishṭhira at the rājasūya), 1926.-[§ 318 (Arjunābhigamanap.): III, 13, 611 (Yuyudhānaḥ, told Kṛshṇa of the gambling)].--§ 320 (Saubhavadhop.): III, 18 [735 (Śiner naptā)], 744 (ºṃ Baladevañ ca ye cānye 'ndhaka-Vṛshṇayaḥ); 21, 833, 836.--[§ 342 (Indralokābhigamanap.): III, 51, 2009 (Yuyudhāna-Bhīmau)].--§ 343 (Nalopākhyānap.): III, 52, 2019.--§ 400 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 118, †10233 (Śineḥ…pautraṃ, came to Yudhishṭhira in Prabhāsa)].--§ 402 (do.): III, 120 (†10259), [†10286 (Śinipravīra)].--[§ 448 (Ājagarap.): III, 176, †12330 (Śineḥ…naptā)].--§ 553 (Vaivāhikap.): IV, 72, 2357 (Yuyudhānaḥ, came to the wedding of Abhimanyu and Uttarā).--§ 554 (Sainyodyogap.): V, [1, †4 (Śinipravīraḥ), †40 (do.)]; 2, (41) (only B.), [55 (Yuyudhānasya)].--[§ 555 (do.): V, 19, 570 (Yuyudhānaḥ, came to Yudhishṭhira with an army)].--§ 556 (Sañjayayānap.): V, 20, 619 (in the army of Yudhishṭhira); 22, [†653 (Sātyakaḥ)], †668; 25, 732; [27, †783 (Yuyudhānaḥ); 28, †804 (Śaineyaḥ)]; 30, †868.--§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 48, [1817 (Śaineyena)], †1852 (Śiner naptāraṃ), †1858 (Mādhavasya); [50, 2006 (Yuyudhānena Vṛshṇivīreṇa)]; 53, 2109; 55, 2204; 57,