Sinīvālī, a goddess (the first day of new moon). § 489 (Āṅgirasa): III, 218, 14126 (Kapardisutā, third daughter of Aṅgiras).--§ 500 (Skandopākhyāna): III, 229, 14451 (Devasenā identified with S.).--§ 606 (Tripurākhyāna): VIII, 34, 1486 (among the auspicious days who became the yoktrāṇi of Śiva's chariot).--§ 615u (Skanda): IX, 45, 2515 (came to the investiture of Skanda).

