Somapada, a tīrtha. § 370 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 84, 8097.

सोमपीथिन्
Somapīthin (“drinker of soma”). § 757o (Hastikūṭa): Gautama said: There where [the sāmans]<BR>Rathantara and Bṛhat are sung, where one strews the altar [C. vedīṃ, B. vedī]<BR>for puṇḍarīkas (sacrifices? so PCR.), where the drinker of soma comes (so B.) with [golden-hued]<BR>steeds (haribhiḥ): XIII, 102, †4896 (only B., instead of upayāti…somapīthī, C. reads upāyānti…Somavīthīṃ).

