Supārśva^1, one or more kings at the time of Yudhishṭhira. § 130 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2665 (incarnation of the Asura Kupatha).--§ 280 (Bhīmasena): II, 30, 1081 (in the east, vanquished by Bhīmasena on his digvijaya).--§ 554 (Sainyodyogap.): V, 4, 77.

सुपार्श्व
Supārśva^2, son of Dhṛtarāshṭra. § 600 (Ghaṭotkacavadhap.): VII, 164, 7337.

सुपर्ण
Suparṇa^1 (“having beautiful wings”) = Garuḍa: I, †724 (grastāṃ Sºsya balena varttikāṃ), 1260 (C. by error Suvº), 1261, (1262), 1304, 1306, 1313 (patageśvaraṃ), 1502, 1518 (origin of the name) 1535, †1544, 1588, 8252 (?ºādyāḥ patatrinaḥ, fight with Kṛshṇa and Arjuna); III, 10574 (pakshirāṭ), 10958(?), 11676 (mahānāgaṃ…sahasāharat), 11680 (ºānilavegena), †15671 (saraḥ Sºena hṛtoragaṃ yathā); V, †2578 (Garuḍaṃ, identified with Kṛshṇa), 3660, 3663, 3675, (3761), (3779), (3801), (3821), 3850, 3874, 3876, 3880, 3884, 3894, 3896, 3917, 4004, 4112, 4022, 4025 (pannagāśanaṃ), 5290 (ºḥ pakshiṇāṃ yathā, sc. senāpatir bhava); VI, 152 (Gº), 208 (Sumukhaḥ…Sºsyātmajaḥ), 3978, 3991 (ºpatane yathā, sc. śabdaḥ); VII, 2572 (ºa iva sāgaraṃ, sc. prāviśat), 2683, 5229 (ºa iva vegena pakshirāṭ), 5532 (ºvegaiḥ…patatribhiḥ), 6343 (rathaṃ…Sºocchritaketanaṃ, i.e. Kṛshṇa's); VIII, 1803 (ºṃ patagaśreshṭhaṃ Vainateyaṃ…bhogīvāhvayase pāte), 1938 (ºvat), †3857 (mahāvanānīva Sºvāyunā, sc. patanti), †4327 (ºvātaprahatā yathoragāḥ); X, 38 (ºm iva vegitaṃ); XII, 8345 (ºārkaracitaṃ …Vaishṇavaṃ padaṃ); XIII, 682 (somahartāraṃ), 4206 (ºsya putraṃ, but read with B. Sºo 'sya putraṃ, and cf. IX, 2669), 6864 (Kaśyapātmajaḥ), 7104 (pannageśvaraḥ, but read patageśvaraḥ with B.); XVI, †62 (the banner (dhvaja) of Kṛshṇa).

सुपर्ण
Suparṇa^2, name of two Devagandharvas. § 101 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 65, 2550 (son of Muni).--§ 102 (do.): I, 65, 2555 (son of Prādhā).

सुपर्ण
Suparṇa^3, an Asura. § 130 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2672 (inearnate as king Kālakīrti).

सुपर्ण
Suparṇa^4 = Sūrya: III, 155.

सुपर्ण
Suparṇa^5, name of a yajus. § 637 (Rājadh.): XII, 47, 1632 (ºo yajur nāma, identified with Krshna; otherwise Nīl. and PCR.).

सुपर्ण
Suparṇa^6, a ṛshi. § 717b (Nārāyanīya): XII, 349, III), 13566 (ṛshiḥ), 13567, 13568 (learnt the religion (dharma) [of Nārāyaṇa]<BR>from Nārāyaṇa himself, and recited it thrice a day, hence it was named trisauparṇa).

सुपर्ण
Suparṇa^7 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सुपर्ण
Suparṇa^8, name of a vyūha. VII, 795 (vyūḍhaṃ), 796. Cf. Garuḍa^2.

सुपर्ण
*Suparṇa, pl. (ºāḥ), birds of Garuḍa's race. I, †722 (dual, said of the Aśvins), 2562, †7011, †7017 (ºnāgāsurasiddhajushṭaṃ, sc. antarīkshaṃ), 8252 (?ºādyāḥ patatriṇah, fought with Kṛshṇa and Arjuna); II, 465 (in the palace of Brahmán), 472 (do.); III, 8214, 10831, 11646, 12924; V, 3586 (lokaḥ Sºānāṃ pakshiṇāṃ pannagāśināṃ, enumeration of the S., sons of Garuḍa); VII, 5641 (ºā iva khecarāḥ), †6921, †9465, 9475; VIII, 2593 (bhakshayanto bhujaṅgamān), †4490 (Brahmarshi-rājarshi-Sºjushṭaṃ, sc. viyat); XI, 453, 778; XII, †1892 (hayaih Sºair iva cāśugāmibhiḥ), 13366; XIII, †1373 (º-Gandharva-Piśāca-Dānavāḥ), 3886 (devāsura-Sºāh) Cf. Garuḍa, pl.

सुपर्णकेतु
Suparṇaketu (“having Garuḍa in his banner”) = Kṛshṇa: III, †12330.

सुपर्णी
suparṇī, said of Svāhā: III, 14308, 14345.

सुपर्वण
Suparvaṇa = Śiva: XIII, 1233 (divi, 1000 names^2).

सुप्रभा
Suprabhā^1, a river, one of the seven Sarasvatīs. § 615i (Saptasārasvata): IX, 38, 2189, 2198 (summoned by Brahmán, the Sarasvatī appeared in Pushkara as S.).

सुप्रभा
Suprabhā^2, a mātṛ. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2628.

सुप्रभा
Suprabhā^3, daughter of Vadānya. § 731b (AshṭāvakraDiks.): XIII, 19, 1392 (married to Ashṭāvakra when he had made a journey to the north).

सुप्रजा
Suprajā, wife of the fire Bhānu. § 493 (Āṅgirasa): III, 221, 14184 (Bhānor bhāryā).

सुप्रजापति
Suprajāpati = Mahāpurusha (Mahāpurushastava).

सुप्रसाद
Suprasāda^1, a warrior of Skanda. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 45, 2573.

सुप्रसाद
Suprasāda^2 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सुप्रसादा
Suprasādā, a mātṛ. § 615 (Skanda): IX, 46, 2631.

सुप्रतर्दन
Supratardana, an ancient king. § 552 (Goharaṇap.) IV, 56, 1768 (came from heaven to see the encounter, BR. proposes to read sa-Pratardanah).

सुप्रतीक
Supratīka^1, an ancient king. § 61 (Anukram.): I, 1, 228 (in Sañjaya's enumeration).

सुप्रतीक
Supratīka^2, the elephant of Bhagadatta. § 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 531.--§ 585 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 95, 4255, 4265, 4276.--§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 26, 1152.

सुप्रतीक
Supratīka^3, a ṛshi, brother of Vibhāvasu. § 41b (Garuḍa): When the ṛshi S. wished to separate from his elder brother Vibhāvasu and make a partition of their patrimony he was cursed by Vibhāvasu, who said: “Thou shalt become an elephant,” and he himself cursed Vibhāvasu, saying: “Thou shalt become a tortoise.” In these forms they continued their hostilities in a lake; the elephant being 6 yojanas in height and 12 in circumference, and the tortoise 3 and 10 respectively (I, 29); I, 29, 1354 (mahātapāḥ), 1355, 1356, 1361, 1362 (º-Vibhāvasū).--§ 42-43 (do.): I, 29--30 (both the elephant and the tortoise were seized and afterwards eaten by Garuḍa).

सुप्रतीक
Supratīka^4, one of the elephants of the quarters. § 564 (Mātalīyop.): V, 99, 3561 (Airāvaṇa, Vāmana, Kumuda, and Añjana were born in the race of S.).--§ 575c (Samā): VI, 12, 475 (description).--§ 599 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 121, 4830 (ºkule jātāḥ, sc. elephants).

सुप्रतिम
Supratima, an ancient king. § 6 (Anukram.): I, 1, 228 (in Sañjaya's enumeration).

सुप्रतिष्ठा
Supratishṭhā, a mātr. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2647.

सुप्रवृद्ध
Supravṛddha, one of the standard-bearers of Jayadratha. § 522 (Draupadīharaṇap.): III, 265, †15597.

सुप्रयोगा
Suprayogā, a river. § 494 (Āṅgirasa): III, 222, 14232 (among the rivers who are mothers of fires).--§ 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 328.

सुप्रिया
Supriyā, an Apsaras. § 104 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 65, 2559 (daughter of Prādhā).--§ 191 (Arjuna): I, 123, 4819 (among the Apsarases who danced at the birth of Arjuna).

सुपुण्ड्रक
Supuṇḍraka, v. Puṇḍraka.

सुपुण्या
Supuṇyā, v. Puṇyā. 

