सूर
Sūra, pl., v. Śūra^8.

सुरा
Surā (“spirituous liquor”, personif.), a goddess. § 28 (Amṛtamanthana): I, 18, 1146 (ºdevī, arose at the churning of the ocean), 1148.--§ 124 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 66, 2616 (suranandinīṃ, daughter of Varuṇa and Devī, the daughter of Śukra).--§ 270 (Brahmasabhāv.): II, 11, 459 (devī, in the palace of Brahmán).

सुरभि
Surabhi or Surabhī, the celestial cow, mother of kine. § 127 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 66, 2625 (daughter of Krodhavaśā), 2631 (mother of Rohiṇī, Gandharvī, Vimalā, and Analā).-§ 164 (Āpavop.): I, 99, 3927 (Dakshasya duhitā…devī, by Kaśyapa, mother of Nandinī, the homa cow of Vasishṭha, (ºī)).--§ 270 (Brahmasabhāv.): II, 11, 457 (devī?, in the palace of Brahmán, (ºī)).--§ 314 (Āraṇyakap.): III, 9, 327, 328, (331), (338), 339 (ºī) (discourse between S. and Indra). --§ 502 (Manushyagrahak.): III, 230, 14486 (gavāṃ mātā, a sickness demon(?) mounted by the demon Śakuni).-§ 564 (Mātalīyop.): V, 102, 3602 (mātā gavām amṛtasambhavā, in Pātāla), 3614 (ºī ksharate payaḥ).--§ 565 (Gālavac.): V, 110, 3810 (ºiḥ ksharate payaḥ, in the west). --§ 668b (Kṛtaghnop.): XII, 173, 6432 (devī Dākshāyaṇī …payasvinī).--§ 730g (Upamanyu): XIII, 14, 715 (ºīgotravarjite, sc. araṇye).--§ 746 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 77, 3712 (mukhajāṃ sutāṃ, sc. Daksha's, (ºī)), 3713 (mother of the saurabheyīs (cows)); 83, 3906 (Dakshasya duhitā devī, (ºī)), (3912) (ºī), 3913 (ºī) (S. performed austerities).-§ 751b (Śapathavidhi): XIII, 94, (4587).--§ 768b (UmāMaheśvarasaṃv.): XIII, 141, 6399 (devadhenuṃ, created by Brahmán, (ºī)).--§ 775 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 166, 7638 (saumyā gauḥ Sºir devī). Cf. Dākshāyaṇī.--Do. pl. (“cows”): XIII, 3754, 3902.

सुरभि
Surabhi = Śiva (1000 names^2). 

सुरभिमत्
Surabhimat, name of a fire. § 493 (Āṅgirasa): III, 221, 14204 (only B., C. has Suramat).

सुरभीपट्टन
Surabhīpaṭṭana, a city. § 284 (Sahadeva): II, 31, 1171 (in the south, conquered by Sahadeva on his digvijaya).

सुरभ्याख्यान
Surabhyākhyāna (“the history of Surabhi”). § 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 423 (i.e. § 314: III, ch. 9).

सुरशत्रु
Suraśatru, pl. (ºavaḥ) (“enemies of the gods”) = Asura, pl.: I, 460; III, 12926; VIII, 1553; IX, 2720; XIII, 4024.--Do. sg.: III, 13614 (i.e. Dhundhu); IX, 2701 (i.e. Bāṇa).

सुरश्रेष्ठ
Suraśreshṭha^1 = Brahmán: VII, 3459; XII, 13074 (only C., B. had Suraśreshṭhāḥ).

सुरश्रेष्ठ
Suraśreshṭha^2 = Śiva: XII, 10399 (1000 names^1), 10435 (do.); XIV, 1889 (Maheśvaraṃ).

सुरश्रेष्ठ
Suraśreshṭha^3 = Indra: I, 2932; III, 8422, 10905 (samarudgaṇaḥ); IX, 2791; XIII, 3180.

सुरश्रेष्ठ
Suraśreshṭha^4 = Nārāyaṇa (Vishṇu): XII, 13159 (Nºṃ Hariṃ).

सुरश्रेष्ठ
Suraśreshṭha^5 = Skanda: III, 14432 (Sº).

सुरश्रेष्ठ
Suraśreshṭha^6 = Sūrya: III, 16986.

सुरश्रेष्ठा
Suraśreshṭhā = Durgā (Umā): IV, 193.

सुरादेवी
Surādevī, v. Surā.

सुराधिप
Surādhipa^1 = Indra, q.v.--Do.^2 = Nahusha, q.v.--Do.^3 pl.: XII, 8251.

सुराध्यक्ष
Surādhyaksha^1 = Śiva (1000 names^2).--Do.^2 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सुरद्विष्
*Suradvish^1, pl. (ºaḥ) (“enemies of the gods”) = Asura, pl.: I, †3230; III, 12214, 12246; VII, 8234, 9560; VIII, 1432 (Asurāḥ), 1459; IX, 2663, 2697, 2699; XII, 6163, 6356.--Do.^2 sg.: III, 16531 (i.e. Rāvaṇa); VII, 1291 (i.e. Bhagadatta).

सुरगण
Suragaṇa = Śiva (1000 names{??}).

सुरगणश्रेष्ठ
Suragaṇaśreshṭha = Vishṇu: V, 413.

सुरगणेश्वर
Suragaṇeśvara = Indra, q.v.

सुरघातिन्
Suraghātin (“slayer of the gods”) = Vṛtra: VII, 3472 (only B.).

सुरगुरु
Suraguru^1 = Brahmán: I, 32(?), 2504.

सुरगुरु
Suraguru^2 = Bṛhaspati: VII, 5648 (only B.); XIII, 5574.

सुरगुरु
Suraguru^3 = Vishṇu (Kṛshṇa): III, 15808 (Vº); VII, 6468(?).

सुरजा
Surajā, an Apsaras. § 103 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 65, 2558 (daughter of Prādhā).

सूरकृत्
Sūrakṛt (B., Suº), son of Viśvāmitra. § 721b (Viśvāmitrop.): XIII, 4, 256.

सुरलोक
