सूर्य
Sūrya^2, an Asura. § 92 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 65, 2534 (ºā-Candramasau, sons of Danu), 2535 (do., not to be confounded with the gods of the same name).--§ 130 (do.): I, 67, 2694 (mahāsuraḥ, incarnate as king Darada). Cf. Asura.

सूर्य
Sūrya^3 = Mahāpurusha (Mahāpurushastava).--Do.^4 = Śiva (1000 names^1--2).--Do.^5 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

सूर्यभास
Sūryabhāsa, a Kuru warrior. § 593 (Abhimanyuvadhap.): VII, 48, 1900 (slain by Abhimanyu).

सूर्यश्री
Sūryaśrī, a Viśvadeva. § 749 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 91, 4358.

सूर्याद
Sūryāda (“devourer of the sun”) = Rāhu(?): XII, 11752.

सूर्यदत्त
Sūryadatta, a follower of Virāṭa. § 552 (Goharaṇap.): IV, 31, 1014 (description of his coat of mail); 32, 1057.-§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 57, 2237 (ºādibhir vīraiḥ, follow Virāṭa).--§ 572 (Rathātirathasaṅkhyānap.): V, 171, 5907 (a ratha in the army of Yudhishṭhira).--§ 600 (Ghaṭotkacavadhap.): VII, 158, 7011 (only B.).--§ 604 (Karṇap.): VIII, 6, 184 (had been slain by Droṇa).

सूर्यध्वज
Sūryadhvaja, a prince. § 232 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 186, 6990 (present at the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).

सूर्यध्वजपताकिन्
Sūryadhvajapatākin = Śiva (1000 names^1).

सूर्यज
