Trigarta, pl. (ºāḥ), a people, especially five brothers, Trigarta princes. § 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 485 (cf. Goharaṇap.). --§ 214 (Hiḍimbavadhap.): I, 156, 6085 (their country visited by the Pāṇḍavas).--§ 279 (Arjuna): II, 27, 1026 (vanquished by Arjuna on his digvijaya).--§ 285 (Nakula): II, 32, 1189 (vanquished by Nakula on his digvijaya).-§ 295 (Dyūtap.): II, 52, 1870 (Śibi-Tº-Yaudheyāḥ, bring tribute to Yudhishṭhira).--§ 522 (Draupadīharaṇap.): III, 271, 15743 (ruled by Kshemaṅkara, they followed Jayadratha).--§ 552 (Goharaṇap.): IV, 25, 868 (mahārathaiḥ), 880 (v. Kīcaka, § 552b); 30, 971 (rājā Tºānāṃ Suśarmā), 981, 993 (Suśarmā…Tºaiḥ sahitaḥ, rob the cattle of Virāṭa); 31, 1007; 32, 1036, 1037, 1055 (C. by error Giº), 1056, 1059, 1060 (rāja Tºānāṃ Suśarmā, encounter between Suśarman and Virāṭa); 33, 1076, 1097, 1101, 1116 (ºānāṃ mahārathe, i.e. Suśarman; Suśarman is made captive); 35, 1149; 38, 1247; 47, 1479; 68, 2161 (jitvā Tºān), 2170, 2171.--§ 556e (Nakula): V, 23, 709 (Nakula had vanquished the Śibis and the T.).--§ 556 (Sañjayayānap.): V, 30, †889 (in Duryodhana's army).--§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 57, 2249 (ºānāñ ca vai mukhyau…Saṃśaptakau).--§ 571 (Ulūkadūtāgamanap.): V, 164, 5709 (the Draupadeyas are pitted against the T. (the five brothers?)).--§ 572 (Rathātirathasaṅkhyānap.): V, 166, 5756 (five brothers who are rathas in Duryodhana's army).--§ 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 368 (in the south(!)).--§ 576 (Bhagavadgītāp.): VI, 20, †754 (in the army of Duryodhana = Saṃśaptaka, pl.?).-§ 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 51, 2097 (protect Bhīshma). --§ 580 (do.): VI, 56, 2405 (B. Traiº, in the head of Bhīshma's gāruḍavyūha).--§ 581 (do.): VI, 61^2, 2691 (attacked Arjuna and Abhimanyu).--§ 582 (do.): VI, 72, 3168 (ºānāṃ rathodarāḥ, fought with Nakula).--§ 584 (do.): VI, 82^2, 3589 (follow Bhīshma).--§ 586 (do.): VI, 99, 4505 (follow Duryodhana); 102, 4660 (Arjuna employed the Vāyavya weapon against the T.).--§ 587 (do.): VI, 114, 5299 (ºānāṃ mahābalaṃ, fought with Arjuna a