Ulūka^1, Kaitavya, son of Śakuni. § 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 515 (ºsya preshaṇaṃ, cf. § 571).--§ 232 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 186, 7002 (Kaitavaḥ, came to the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).-§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 47, 1799; 57, 2254 (Nakula wished to fight U.).--§ 571 (Ulūkadūtāgamanap.): V, 160, 5412 (Kaitavya), 5471, 5476, 5484, 5486; 161, 5537, (5540); 162, 5578, 5586, 5588, 5596, 5616, 5621, 5626, 5629 (Kaitavya); 163, 5666 (Kaitavyaṃ), 5673, 5679, 5683, 5684, 5688 (Kaitavyaṃ), 5692, 5693, 5695; 164, 5702 (U. was sent by Duryodhana as an ambassador to the Pāṇḍavas).--§ 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 45^21, 1747, 1748 (fought with the Cedi king).--§ 582 (do.): VI, 72, 3166 (Śakunim Uºñ ca…pitāpitrau, attacked by Sahadeva). --§ 583 (do.): VI, 79, 3456 (all. to § 571).--§ 600 (Ghaṭotkacavadhap.): VII, 171, 7715 (son of Śakuni, pierced by Arjuna), 7718.--§ 603 (Nārāyaṇāstramokshap.): VII, 193, 8906.--[§ 604 (Karṇap.): VIII, 7, †208 (Kaitavyānām adhipaḥ).]--§ 605 (do.): VIII, 11, 414 (Śakuni and U. in the eyes of the makaravyūha of Karṇa); 25, 993, 994, 995, 998, 1000, 1001, 1004 (encounter with Yudhishṭhira).--§ 608 (do.): VIII, 46, 2134 (Śakuni and U. were followed by the Gāndhāras); 48, 2263 (brother of Patatri, PCR.); 54, 2610; 61, 3078 (attacked by Sahadeva), 3108, 3110, 3115.--§ 609 (Śalyap.): IX, 1, 26 (Kaitavaḥ, among the slain).--§ 611 (do.): IX, 8, 400; 11, 563 (C. has by error Ūº); 22, 1157 (encounter with Nakula; Saubalasya sutaṃ, v. 1158); 27, 1459; 28, 1503, 1528, 1532 (slain by Sahadeva). Cf. the following synonyms:-Śākuni (“the son of Śakuni”): VIII, 997. Kaitava (“the gambler's son”): I, 7002 (Uº); V, 5665. Kaitavya (do.): V, 2254 (Uº), 5412 (Uº), 5535, 5579, 5582, 5583, 5628, 5629 (Uº), 5643, 5644, †5651, 5666 (Uº), 5671, 5688 (Uº), 5698; IX, 26 (Uº, has been slain), 96, 394.

