Urvaśī^1, an Apsaras, wife of Purūravas. § 52 (Janamejaya): I, 44, †1811 (yathoºīṃ prāpya purā Purūravāḥ).--§ 135 (Śakuntalop.): I, 74, 3055 (among the principal Apsarases). --§ 140 (Purūravas): I, 75, 3148 (wife of Purūravas).-§ 141 (do.): I, 75, 3149 (ºsutāḥ; by Purūravas, mother of six sons, Āyus, etc.).--§ 19 (Arjuna): I, 123, 4823 (sung at the birth of Arjuna).--§ 269 (Vaiśravaṇasabhāv.): II, 10, 393 (among the Apsarases in the palace of Kubera).-§ 336 (Indralokābhigamanap.): III, 43, 1784 (in the palace of Indra); 45, 1800, 1801, 1803, 1814; 46, 1817, 1833, 1835, 1837, (1838), (1858), 1864, (1865), 1867, 1868, 1872 (U. fell in love with Arjuna; as he refused her she cursed him saying that he should become a woman).-§ 391 (Ṛshyaśṛṅga): III, 110, 10002 (Apsarasaṃ, when Vibhāṇḍaka saw U. his seed come out).--§ 565 (Gālavacar.): V, 117, 3973 (reme…yathā…Uºyāñ ca Purūravāḥ). --§ 595 (Shoḍaśarāj. v. Bhagīratha): VII, 60, 2254 (seems to be identified with the heavenly Gaṅgā, tathā Bhāgīrathī Gaṅgā Urvaśī cābhavatpurā).--§ 632b (Shoḍaśarāj., v. § 595): XII, 29, 961 (do., Gaṅgā Bhāgīrathī tasmād Urvaśī hy abhavat purā).--§ 716 (Śukābhipatana): XII, 333, 12577, 12601.--§ 731b (Ashṭāvakra-Diksaṃv.): XIII, 19, 1424 (in the abode of Kubera).--§ 775 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 166, 7641.

