वैशेषिक
Vaiśeshika, adj. (“relating to the Vaiśeshika-doctrine”?): XII, 1658 (guṇaiḥ, probably a wrong reading; cf. PCR. and his note on XII, 11874).

वैश्रवण
Vaiśravaṇa^1 = Kubera, q.v.--Do.^2 = Śiva (1000 names^2).

वैश्रवण
Vaiśravaṇa, adj. (“belonging to Vaiśravaṇa [i.e. Kubera]”). § 269 (Vaiśravaṇasabhāv.): II, 10, 383 (sabhā…Vºī).-§ 641 (Rājadh.): XII, 124, 4561 (ṛddhiṃ…Vºīṃ).

वैश्रवणसभावर्णन
Vaiśravaṇa-sabhā-varṇana(ṃ) (“description of the palace of Kubera”). § 269 (Lokapālas.): The sabhā of Vaiśravaṇa (i.e. Kubera) is 100 yojanas in length and 70 in breadth, acquired by Vaiśravaṇa by his ascetic power; it is supported by Guhyakas attached to the firmament, and capable of moving along it. There sits Vaiśravaṇa with thousands of wives, amidst the fragrance of the lotuses of the nalinī Alakā and the Nandana gardens, and the gods, Gandharvas (those called Kinnaras and those called Naras), Apsarases (enumeration), Yakshas (enumeration), Lakshmī, Nalakūbara, myself (i.e. Nārada), many devarshis and brahmarshis, kravyādas (i.e. Rākshasas), Umāpati (i.e. Śiva), with hosts of spirits (bhūtasaṅghaiḥ, dwarfs, etc.), and Devī (i.e. Umā), and Gandharva chiefs (enumeration), and Cakradharman, the chief of the Vidyādharas, Bhagadatta, and innumerable other kings, and Druma, the chief of the Kimpurushas, and the Rākshasa king Mahendra Gandhamādana (according to BR., who takes it to be = Rāvaṇa), and Vibhīshaṇa (the brother of Kubera), and the mountains Himavat, etc. (enumeration), in their personified forms, and Nandīśvara and Mahākāla, and many pārishadas with arrowy ears and mouths, Kāshṭha, Kuṭīmukha, Dantin, and Vijayā (B. Vijaya), and the roaring white bull [of Śiva, PCR.], and Piśācas. Paulastya (i.e. Kubera) always adores Śiva, and sometimes is honoured by his visit. There also the best of jewels, Śaṅkha and Padma, those princes of all gems [in their personified forms, PCR.], accompanied by all the jewels of the earth, worship Kubera (II, 10).

वैश्वदेव
Vaiśvadeva, adj. (“belonging to the Viśvadevas”). § 677 (Mokshadh.): XII, 244, 8871 (sc. loke).--§ 704 (do.): XII, 302, 11105 (vishayān).--§ 746 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 60, 3060 (tṛtīyaṃ savanaṃ); 79, 3775 (sthānaṃ, C. has by error Vaiśyaº).--§ 778b (Saṃvartta-Maruttīya): XIV, 10, †285 (ukshāṇaṃ).--§ 782g (Guruśishyasaṃv.): XIV, 42, 1129 (vāc).--Do.^2, subst. neutr. (do.), name of a certain offering. § 309 (Āraṇyakap.): III, 2, 105.--§ 327 (Draupadīparitāpav.): III, 30, 1130.--§ 732 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 22, 1553.--§ 753 (do.): XIII, 97, 4659, 4660, 4667, 4673.

वैश्वामित्र
Vaiśvāmitra (“son of viśvāmitra”) = Ashṭaka: III, †13301 (Aº).

वैश्वानर
Vaiśvānara^1 = Agni, q.v. (Add VII. 2019; VIII, 2160; for II, 299, see next.)

वैश्वानर
Vaiśvānara^2, a muni. § 266 (Śakrasabhāv.): II, 7, 299 (muniḥ, in the palace of Indra).

वैश्वानर
Vaiśvānara, pl. (ºāḥ), a class of ṛshis. § 656 (Khaḍgotpattik.): XII, 166, 6143 (º-Marīcipāḥ).

वैश्वानरमुख
Vaiśvānaramukha = Śiva: XIV, 201.

वैश्वानरी
Vaiśvānarī, adj. f. (“belonging to [Agni]<BR>Vaiśvānara”) said of the Earth. § 746 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 62, 3140 (C. by error Vaiśyānarī).

वैश्याः
Vaiśyāḥ (pl.) = Śiva (1000 names^1).

वैश्यापुत्र
Vaiśyāputra (“the son of a vaiśya woman”) = Yuyutau, q.v.

वैदम्भ
Vaidambha = Śiva (1000 names^2).

वैदर्भ
Vaidarbha (“the king of the Vidarbhas”), the father of Lopāmudrā. § 382 (Agastyop.): III, 96, 8562; 97, 8570.

वैदर्भि
Vaidarbhi (do.), the father of Lopāmudrā. § 767 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 137, 6255 (gave his daughter to Agastya).

वैदर्भी
Vaidarbhī^1 (“the daughter of the king of the Vidarbhas”) = Suśravā: I, ††3770 (Sº).

वैदर्भी
Vaidarbhī^2 (do.) = Maryādā: I, ††3771 (Mº).

वैदर्भी
Vaidarbhī^3 (do.) = Damayantī: III, 2146, 2156, 2164, 2181, 2201, 2203, 2261, 2337, 2351, 2410, 2458, 2568, 2642, 2660, 2678, 2681, 2762, 2775, 2886, 2896, 2910, 2911, 2955, 3002 (ºjananī), 3005, 3009, 3050, 3065.

वैदर्भी
Vaidarbhī^4 (do.) = Lopāmudrā: III, 8569 (yuvatīṃ); V, 3971 (reme…yathā Agastyaś cāpi Vºyāṃ).

वैदर्भी
Vaidarbhī^5 (do.), wife of Sagara. § 387 (Sagara): III, 106, 8833, 8843 (bore a gourd, from which arose sixty thousands of sons).

वैदेह
Vaideha^1 (“the king of the Videhas”), a prince contemporary with Yudhishṭhira. § 264 (Sabhākriyāp.): II, 4, 122 (waited upon Yudhishṭhira).

वैदेह
Vaideha^2 (do.) = Janaka: XII, 835 (Jº), 3909, 3937, 3955, 10876, 10916, 11434 (i.e. Karālajanaka), 11840 (Jº), 11842.

वैदेह
Vaideha^3 (do.) = Nimi: XII, 8600 (Nº).

वैदेह
Vaideha^4, pl. (ºāḥ), a people = Videha, pl. § 280 (Bhīmasena): II, 30, 1089 (ºsthaḥ, sc. Bhīmasena; on his digviyaya Bhīmasena conquered V. and therefrom sent expeditions).-§ 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 364.--§ 608 (Karṇap.): VIII, 79, 4040 (ºāmbashṭha-Kāmbojāḥ, had been vanquished by Arjuna in the battle).

वैदेह
Vaideha^5, name of a mixed caste: XIII, 2582 (sg.), 2589 (ºyāṃ, fem.).

वैदेहक
Vaidehaka, name of a mixed caste = Vaideha: XII, 10868 (pl.); XIII, 2571 (sg.), 2585 (do.), 2587 (do.).

वैदेहक
Vaidehaka, adj. (“belonging to the Videhas”). § 280 (Bhīmasena): II, 30, 1087 (ºṃ rājānaṃ Janakaṃ). 

वैदेही
Vaidehī^1 (“the daughter of the king of the Videhas”) = Maryādā: I, ††3776 (Mº).

वैदेही
Vaidehī^2 (do.), the wife of Śatānīka^2 (the son of Janamejaya). § 160 (Pūruvaṃś.): I, 95, ††3838.

वैदेही
