Vasudāna, king of Pāṃśurāshṭra. § 264 (Sabhākriyāp.): II, 4, 122 (waited upon Yudhishṭhira).--§ 295 (Dyūtap.): II, 52, 1884 (Pāṃśurāshṭrāt, gave tribute to Yudhishṭhira). --§ 296 (do.): II, 53, 1914.--§ 570 (Sainyaniryāṇap.): V, 151, 5161 (in the army of Yudhishṭhira).--§ 572 (Rathātirathasaṅkhyānap.): V, 171, 5919 (do., is an atiratha).-§ 573 (Ambopākhyānap.): V, 196, 7650 (followed Yudhishṭhira).--§ 578 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 51, 2110.--§ 585 (do.): VI, 93, 4151 (followed Bhīmasena); 95, 4255.-§ 592 (Saṃśaptakavadhap.): VII, 21, 903, 909 (slain by Droṇa); 23, 990 (followed Dhṛstadyumna, description of his horses).--§ 599 (Jayadrathavadhap.): VII, 113, 4374.-§ 602 (Droṇavadhap.): VII, 190, 8724 (slain by Droṇa).-§ 604 (Karṇap.): VIII, 6, 174 (the son of V. had slain Abhibhu the Kāśi king in the battle(!)), 188 (had been slain by Droṇa). Cf. Pāṃśurāshṭrādhipa.

