Viśvāvasu, a Gandharva king. § 21 (Pramadvarā): I, 8, 943 (Gandharvarājaḥ, begot Pramadvarā on Menakā).--§ 102 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 65, 2555 (among the Devagandharvas, sons of Prādhā).--§ 191 (Arjuna): I, 123, 4814 (among the Devagandharvas present at the birth of Arjuna).--§ 221b (Cākshushī): I, 170, 6478 (learnt the Cākshushī from Soma and communicated it to Citraratha).--§ 233 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 187, †7011 (came to see the svayaṃvara of Draupadī).-§ 266 (Śakrasabhāv.): II, 7, 303 (in the palace of Indra).-§ 269 (Vaiśravaṇasabhāv.): II, 10, 406 (Gandharvāṇāñ ca patayo Vºuḥ, etc., in the palace of Kubera).--§ 336 (Indralokābhigamanap.): III, 43, 1773 (ºprabhṛtibhir Gandharvaiḥ).--§ 377 (Dhaumyatīrthak.): III, 90, 8389 (a śloka sung by V. quoted, PCR. has Vibhāvasu).--§ 378 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 91, 8420 (ºos tu tanayād, i.e. Citrasena).-§ 443 (Nivātakavacayuddhap.): III, 168, 12048 (ºoś ca vai putraś Citrasenaḥ).--§ 530 (Viśvāvasumokshaṇa): III, 279, 16086 (Gandharvaḥ, had been cursed and become a Rākshasa (Kabandha), but was delivered by Rāma Dāśarathi).--§ 555 (Indravijaya): V, 11, 356 (ºur Nāradaś ca).--§ 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 6, 214 (on Meru).--§ 595 (Shoḍaśarāj., v. Dilīpa): VII, 61, v. 7 (only B. in a śloka wanting in C. after v. 2266; played on his vīṇā at the sacrifice of Dilīpa). § 615d (Gandharvānāṃ tīrthaṃ): IX, 37, 2128 (ºmukhāḥ …Gandharvāḥ).--§ 632b (Shoḍaśarāj., cf. § 595, v. Dilīpa): XII, 29, 969 (played on his vīṇā at the sacrifice of Dilīpa). --§ 662b (Jāpakop.): XII, 200, 7340.--§ 694b (Jvarotpatti): XII, 284, 10218 (Gandharvaḥ).--§ 695b (Dakshayajñavināśa): XII, 285, 10279.--§ 707 (Mokshadh.): XII, 319, 11750 (Gandharvaḥ), 11759, 11771, (11781), (†11807) (was instructed by Yājñavalkya).--§ 712 (Śukotpatti): XII, 324, 12176 (Gandharvaḥ); 325, 12201 (do.). --§ 730 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 16, 1050 (?º-HiraṇyākshaPuruhātanamaskṛta, sc. Śiva).--§ 746 (do.): XIII, 83, 3887.--§ 775 (do.): XIII, 166, 7639.--§ 785 (Anugītāp.): XIV, 88, 2642.--§ 786e (Agastya): XIV, 92, 2871.- § 789 (Putradarśanap.): XV, 29, 774. Cf. Gandharva, Gandharvarāja, Gandharvendra, Kāśyapa.

