वृषामित्र
Vṛshāmitra, a brahman. § 324 (Dvaitavanapr.): III, 26, 987 (waited upon Yudhishṭhira).

वृषण
Vṛshaṇa = Śiva (1000 names^2).

वृषनाभ
Vṛshanābha = Śiva: VII, 9530.

वृषाण्ड
Vṛshāṇḍa, an Asura(?). § 673b (Bali-Vāsavasaṃv.): XII, 227, 8265 (among the ancient rulers of the earth).

वृषाङ्क
Vṛshāṅka = Śiva, q.v.

वृषपर्वन्
Vṛshaparvan^1, a rājarshi. § 11 (Parvasaṅgr.): I, 2, 455.--§ 434 (Saugandhikāharaṇa): III, 156, 11444 (āśramaṃ Vºṇaḥ; c: the hermitage of V. is inhabited by Siddhas and Cāraṇas).--§ 436 (Yakshayuddhap.): III, 158, 11543 (āśramaṃ Vºṇaḥ), 11544 (rājarshiṃ), 11546, 11547, 11549 (āśrame Vºṇaḥ), 11551, 11552 (the Pāṇḍavas, etc., came to the hermitage of V. on the Himavat; V. showed them the way [to the mountain Śveta]), 11556 (yathoktaṃ Vºṇā), 11620 (do.).--§ 449 (Ājagarap.): III, 177, †12344 (āśramāgryaṃ Vºṇaḥ, the Pāṇḍavas, etc., returned to the hermitage of V.), †12345 (the hermitage of V. is frequented by gods and maharshis).--§ 450 (do.): III, 178, 12366 (āśramāt…rājarsher Vºṇaḥ).

