Vṛshaparvan^2, an Asura chief. § 92 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 65, 2532 (among the sons of Danu).--§ 130 (do.): I, 67, 2651 (mahāsuraḥ, incarnate as king Dīrghaprajña), 2652 (elder brother of Ajaka).--§ 145 (Kaca): I, 76, 3185 (ŚukraVºau), 3195 (had Śukra as his purohita).--§ 146 (Devayānī): I, 78, 3284 (Śarmishṭhā…duhitā Vºṇaḥ), 3303 (nagaraṃ Vºṇaḥ), 3305 (Śarmishṭhayā…duhitrā Vºṇaḥ), 3309 (do.), 3312 (Śarmishṭhā…duhitā Vºṇaḥ), 3315; 79, 3330 (duhitur Vºṇaḥ, i.e. Śarmishṭhā), 80, 3332, 3336, (3338), (3342), 3344 (mahākaviḥ), (3346), (3348), 3356 (duhitrā Vºṇaḥ, i.e. Śarmishṭhā); 81, 3368 (duhitā Dānavendrasya Śarmishṭhā Vºṇaḥ) (when Śarmishṭhā, the daughter of V., had ill-used Devayānī, the daughter of Śukra, V. appeased her and Śukra by giving her Śarmishṭhā as a maidservant).--§ 147 (do.): I, 82, 3398 (sutāṃ…Vºṇaḥ, i.e. Śarmishṭhā); 83, 3451 (Śarmishṭhayā…duhitrā Vºṇaḥ). --§ 156 (Pūruvaṃś.): I, 95, ††3761 (ºṇaś ca duhitā Śarmishṭhā).--§ 263 (Sabhākriyāp.): II, 3, 60 (sabhāyāṃ Vºṇaḥ), 75 (sabhādravyaṃ Vºṇaḥ, Maya brought various precious articles from the palace of V. in the north for the construction of the palace of Yudhishṭhira).--§ 569b (Yayāti): V, 149, 5044 (Śarmishṭhayā…duhitrā Vºṇaḥ). Cf. Asura, Daitya, Dānavendra.

