व्यास
Vyāsa^2 = Śiva (1000 names^2).--Do.^3 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

व्यासशिष्य
Vyāsaśishya (“the disciple of Vyāsa”) = Vaiśampāvana: I, 303; II, 1788/89 (only B.); XV, 922.

व्यासस्थली
Vyāsasthalī, name of a sacred place (tīrtha). § 364 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 83, 6066.

व्यासात्मज
Vyāsātmaja (“the son of Vyāsa”) = Śuka: XII, 13647.

व्यासवन
Vyāsavana, name of a sacred forest. § 364 (Tīrthayātrāp.): III, 83, 6063.

व्यवसाय
Vyavasāya^1 (“eternal law”, personif.). § 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2682.--§ 641 (Rājadh.): XII, 122, 4512 (Brahmaṇaḥ putraḥ), 4513.--Do.^2 = Śiva (1000 names^1--2).-Do.^3 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

व्यवस्थान
Vyavasthāna(ṃ) = Vishṇu (1000 names).

व्यय
Vyaya, name of a serpent. § 67 (Sarpasattra): I, 57, 2157 (of Dhṛtarāshṭra's race; read with B. Avyaya, q.v.).

व्योमगङ्गा
Vyomagaṅgā (“the heavenly Gaṅgā”). § 714 (Śukakṛtya): XII, 329, 12421.

व्योमकेश
Vyomakeśa = Śiva: VII, 9626.

व्योमन्
Vyoman = Mahāpurusha (Mahāpurushastava).

व्योमारि
Vyomāri, a Viśvadeva. § 749 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 91, 4360.

व्यूक
Vyūka, pl. (ºāḥ), a people. § 574 (Jambūkh.): VI, 9, 369 (only B., C. has Bakāḥ).

व्यूढोरस्क
Vyūḍhoraska, son of Dhṛtarāshṭra. § 585 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 96, 4345 (slain by Bhīmasena). Cf. next.

व्यूढोरु
Vyūḍhoru, son of Dhṛtarāshṭra. § 130 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2740.--§ 182 (Dhṛtarāshṭraputranāmak.): I, 117, 4553 (B. Vyūḍhoraḥ).

व्यूहशास्त्र
*vyūhaśāstra (“the science of arrays”): VI, 3866.

व्युषिताश्व
Vyushitāśva, an ancient king, descendant of Pūru. § 186b (Pāṇḍu): There was a king named Vyushitāśva, of the race of Pūru; once, when he sacrificed, the gods, with Indra and Devarshis, came there, and the gods and the Brahmarshis began themselves to perform a sacrifice (cakruḥ karma svayaṃ); having subdued the eastern, northern, western, and southern princes, he performed a horse-sacrifice (a gāthā from the Purāṇas is cited), etc. The wife of V. was Bhadrā Kākshīvatī, whom he loved so much that he was attacked by phthisis and died sonless; Bhadrā could not bear separation from him and cried out that he should show himself to her; then his voice was heard saying that she, having bathed, should lie down with him on her bed on the night of the eighth or fourteenth day of the moon, then he would beget offspring upon her. By the corpse of her husband she gave birth to seven children: three Śālvas and four Madras: I, 121, 4686 (Pūror vaṃśavivardhanaḥ), 4688 (rājarsheḥ), 4689, 4691, 4692, 4693.--§ 187 (do.): I, 122, 4717. Y

यशस्
Yaśas = Śiva (1000 names^2).

यशस्विनी
Yaśasvinī, a mātṛ. § 615u (Skanda): IX, 46, 2628.

यशोदा
Yaśodā, wife of the cowherd Nanda. § 549f (Durgā): IV, 6, 179 (ºgarbhasambhūtāṃ, sc. Durgā; cf. Harivaṃśa v. 3313 foll.).

यशोधर
Yaśodhara, son of Kṛshṇa and Rukmiṇī. § 730 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 14, 621 (so. B., C. has Yaśovaraḥ).

यशोधरा
Yaśodharā, a Trigarta princess. § 156 (Pūruvaṃś.): I, 95, ††3788 (Traigartīṃ, wife of Hastin and mother of Vikuṇṭhana).

यशोवर
Yaśovara (XIII, 621), v. Yaśodhara.

यशोवासस्
Yaśovāsas = Mahāpurusha (Mahāpurushastava).

यद्
Yad (or Yat-tad) = Vishṇu (1000 names).

