युग
Yuga(ṃ) = Śiva (1000 names^1).

युगाधिप
Yugādhipa = Śiva (1000 names^2).

युगादि
Yugādi = Mahāpurusha (Mahāpurushastava).

युगादिकृत्
Yugādikṛt = Vishṇu (1000 names).

युगाग्नि
Yugāgni = Kṛshṇa (Vishṇu): VI, 2954 (only C.).

युगमध्य
Yugamadhya = Mahāpurusha (Mahāpurushastava).

युगन्धर
Yugandhara^1, name of a place. § 409 (Plakshāvata raṇagamana): III, 129, 10521 (ºs dadhi prāśya).--§ 607 (Karṇap.): VIII, 44, 2062 (ºe payaḥ pītvā, in the country of the Bāhīkas?).

युगन्धर
Yugandhara^2, a Pāṇḍava warrior. § 590 (Droṇābhishekap.): VII, 16, 648 (attacked Droṇa), 649 (slain by Droṇa).

युगन्धर
Yugandhara^3, pl. (ºāḥ), a people. § 549 (Pāṇḍavapraveśap.): IV, 1, 12.

युगनिधन
Yuganidhana = Mahāpurusha (Mahāpurushastava).

युगप
Yugapa, a Gandharva. § 191 (Arjuna): I, 123, 4812 (among the Devagandharvas present at the birth of Arjuna).

युगरूप
Yugarūpa, Yugāvaha = Śiva (1000 names^2).

युगावर्त
Yugāvarta^1 = Śiva (1000 names^1).--Do.^2 = Vishṇu (1000 names).

युक्त
Yukta, Yuktabāhu = Śiva (1000 names^2).

यूपध्वज
Yūpadhvaja (XI, 681, 691, 692), Yūpaketana, Yūpaketu (also XI, 686) = Bhūriśravas, q.v.

युवन्
Yuvan = Śiva (1000 names^1)

युवनाश्व
Yuvanāśva, an ancient king. § 6 (Anukramanikāp.): I, 1, 226 (in Sañjaya's enumeration).--§ 407 (Māndhātrup.): III, 126, 10427 (Ikshvākuvaṃśaprabhavaḥ), 10441, 10451 (Y. bore Māndhātṛ, who came out piercing his left side).-§ 475 (Dhundhumārop.): III, 202, 13517 (king of Ayodhyā, son of Adri and father of Śrāva).--§ 595 (Shoḍaśarāj., v. Māndhātṛ): VII, 62, 2274 (ºsya jaṭhare, birth of Māndhātṛ, cf. § 407).--§ 632b (Shoḍaśarāj., cf. § 595): XII, 29, 975 (do., do.).--§ 655 (Āpaddh.): XII, 159, 5924 (acquired heaven).--§ 656 (Khaḍgotpattik.): XII, 166, 6197 (received the sword from Raivata, from him it passed over to Raghu).--§ 677 (Mokshadh.): XII, 235, 8599 (attained to heaven by way of gifts, PCR. connects Y. with Vṛshādarbhi, but probably wrongly; cf. XIII, 6254).--§ 761 (Ānuśāsanik.): XIII, 115, 5663 (abstained from meat during the month of Kārttika). Cf. Saudyumni.

युवराजाचेदीनां
Yuvarājā Cedīnāṃ (“the crown prince of the Cedis”): VII, 9330 (cf. 9336, †9337, †9342, 9343 (slain by Aśvatthāman), 9400).

युयुधान
Yuyudhāna = Sātyaki, q.v.

युयुत्सु
Yuyutsu, son of Dhṛtarāshṭra and a vaiśyā. § 83 (Ādivaṃśāvatāraṇa): I, 63, 2446 (karaṇaḥ), (), 2448 (Vaiśyāputraḥ,) among eleven sons of Dhṛtarāshṭra who are mahārathas).--§ 130 (Aṃśāvat.): I, 67, 2726 (d: Vaiśyāputraḥ…Dhārtarāshṭraḥ śatādhikaḥ), 2728, 2741 (Vaiśyā-putraḥ…Dhārtarāshṭraḥ śatādhikaḥ).--§ 180 (Gāndhārīputrotpatti): I, 115, 4521 (karaṇaḥ, born from a vaiśyā), 4522 (Vaiśyāputraḥ).--§ 181 (Duḥśalotpatti): I, 116, 4524 (do.).--§ 182 (Dhṛtarāshṭraputranāmak.): I, 117, 4541 (enumeration of the sons of Dhṛtarāshṭra).--[§ 197 (Bhīmasenarasapāna): I, 129, 5067/8 (only B., Vaiśyāputraḥ).]-§ 209 (Drupadaśāsana): I, 138, 5449--§ 232 (Svayaṃvarap.): I, 186, 6982 (came to the svayaṃvara of Draupadī). [§ 302 (Anudyūtap.): II, 74, 2476 (Vaiśyāputraḥ).]--§ 305 (do.): II, 78, 2562.--§ 327 (Draupadīparitāpav.): III, 29, 1112.--§ 556 (Sañjayayānap.): V, 23, †697 (Vaiśyāputraḥ).--§ 561 (Yānasandhip.): V, 47, 1797; 61, 2410 (according to Nīl.).--§ 562 (Bhagavadyānap.): V, 95, 3404.--§ 567 (do.): V, 131, 4457.--§ 571 (Ulūkadūtāgamanap.): V, 160, 5531 (ºtoyaṃ, sc. purushodudhiṃ, i.e. the army of Duryodhana, only C.).--§ 577 (Bhīshmavadhap.): VI, 43, 1623, 1625, 1628 (joined the Pāṇḍavas).--§ 589 (Droṇābhishekap.): VII, 8, 228; 10, 364 (f: at Vāraṇāvata many wrathful kings battling together for six months, desiring to slay Y., could not vanquish him).--§ 592 (Saṃcaptakavadhap.): VII, 23, 984 (cf. 1024 [v. Additions s.v. Bṛhanta], proceeded against Droṇa, description of his norses); 25, 1076 (fought with his brother Subāhu), 1078; 26, 1180, 1183, (), 1186 (fought with the elephant of Bhagadatta).--§ 596 (Pratijñāp.): VII, 72, 2536.-§ 597 (do.): VII, 83, 2951 (Kauravyaṃ).--§ 605 (Karṇap.): VIII, 25, 993, 994, 996, 999 (ºoḥ kāñcanadhvajaḥ), 1000, 1002 (vanquished by Ulūka); 30, 1231 (attacked Karṇa).--§ 608 (do.): VIII, 49, 2333 (attacked Vasusheṇa).--§ 612 (Hradapraveśap.): IX, 29, 1645, (1658), 1663, 1668, 1671 (returned to Hāstinapura).--§ 615 (Gadāyuddhap.): IX, 62, 3461.--§ 618 (Jalapradānikap.): XI, 12, 315.--§ 620 (Śrāddhap.): XI, 26, 780 (among those whom Yudhishṭhira ordered to perform the funeral rites for the dead warriors).--§ 635 (Rājadh.): XII, 37, 1381 (accompanied Yudhishṭhira).--§ 637 (do.): XII, 40, 1448; 41, 1483; 43, 1529; 44, 1541 (Dhārtarāshṭrasya); 47, 1695 (proceeded to see Bhīshma).--§ 777 (Svargārohaṇik. p.): XIII, 168, 7715; 169, 7769, 7771 (present when Bhīshma ascended to heaven).--§ 783 (Anugītāp.): XIV, 52, 1504; 60, 1805 (Kauravyaḥ, all. to the battle); 63, 1894 (Kauravyaṃ…Dhrtarāshtrajam, remained in Hāstinapura while the Pāṇḍavas fetched the gold); 66, 1942; [71, 2061 (Vaiśyāputraṃ)].--§ 787 (Āśramavāsap.): XV, 1, 5 (Vaiśyāputraḥ), 12; 3, 107; 4, 168; 16, 445. --§ 788 (do.): XV, 23, 632 (remained in Hāstinapura while the Pāṇḍavas visited Dhṛtarāshṭra, etc.).--§ 792 (Nāradāgamanap.): XV, 39, 1089 (performed the funeral rites for Dhṛtarāshṭra, etc.).--§ 794 (Mahāprasthānikap.): XVII, 1, 6 (Vaiśyāputre, Yudhishṭhira made over the kingdom to Y., Parikshit being installed on the throne), 27. Cf. also the following synonyms:-Dhārtarāshṭra, Dhṛtarāshṭraja, Dhrtarāshṭrasuta, q.v. Karaṇa, q.v. Kaurava, Kauravya, q.v. Vaiśyāputra (“the son of a vaiśyā”): I, 2448 (Yº), 2726 (Yº), 2741 (Yº), 4522 (Yº), 4524 (Yº), 5067/8 (only B.); II, 2476; VII, 2539; IX, 1652, 1662; XIV, 2061 XV, 5 (Yº), †435; XVII, 6 (Yº). blank blank 


